(window.StoryDialogue = window.StoryDialogue || {})["ev-11"] = {"561301101":[["","Dawnstar League, Underground Research Facility"],["","The research facility is newly built. Brand-new instruments gleam with a cold metallic sheen, and the dust of history has yet to gather in its hidden corners."],["","This should be the busiest time for the research facility, yet it is eerily deserted. In the silence, only the occasional beep of an instrument breaks through."],["","Most of the staff have been reassigned due to a special guest today, leaving only one person sitting at the reception desk at the entrance, occasionally glancing at the monitor and clock."],["","Shawnee Russell, the DL's newly appointed head of security, is waiting for something. Only someone nervous would watch the time so closely."],["Shawnee","They're here...? Much earlier than expected."],["","The instant the metal doors slide open, a mountain of a man strides in. The heavy thud of military boots sends the air taut."],["Leopold","...Oh? I thought it would be that guy himself..."],["Shawnee","A pleasure to meet you, Lieutenant Colonel Leopold. I'm..."],["Leopold","Shawnee Russell, right?"],["","Leopold takes Shawnee's outstretched hand, cutting off her introduction as he does."],["Leopold","I heard your inaugural address on the broadcast. You're the newly appointed... head of security for East Milkhama? Ha-ha! That title didn't exist before, did it?"],["Shawnee","That's right. The position was established to address any friction that might arise between East and West Milkhama..."],["Leopold","Good. The war is over. The military can't keep stepping in every time something happens. The DL needs someone who can speak for it beyond its borders."],["Leopold","And you being here means... you're one of his people too?"],["Shawnee","...I think you've misunderstood."],["","They release each other's hands at the same moment."],["Shawnee","I don't know how the military's internal factions stand these days, nor do I care. I'm here as the person responsible for negotiating the Nova Project."],["Leopold","I see... But you know, there are two kinds of people in the military: normal people, and those who always use the mission as an excuse to run away."],["Leopold","So this is your roundabout way of declaring your allegiance."],["Shawnee","..."],["Shawnee","With respect, that is the most dangerous mindset a soldier can have..."],["Leopold","Shawnee, you're no soldier, but you've seen the absurd missions people have fought wars over on this island..."],["Shawnee","That's why we need this Nova Project now."],["","This time, Shawnee is the one who cuts Leopold off. Her patience only stretches so far."],["Shawnee","Leopold, everything I've heard says you're a reasonable man."],["Shawnee","The UNCS suddenly has a mysterious Super Pilot of unknown origin—the Valkyrie. She's been crushing our front-line forces, inflicting devastating losses... including on one of your own squads. Only one member survived."],["Shawnee","Without a force strong enough to preserve the balance, this hard-won peace will only be shattered again."],["Leopold","I know that better than anyone..."],["Shawnee","Then let's stop wasting time... You may have been the contact for that operation, but you aren't the one signing this agreement. That would be..."],["???","May I speak?"],["","An unexpected voice cuts in, drawing Shawnee's attention to the third person in the room."],["","When did she come in...? No—she has been behind Leopold from the start, hidden from view by his massive frame."],["","After that, Shawnee's attention remains fixed on Leopold, the man she has to look up at, and she overlooks the third person beside him... the one she has to look down at."],["","A little girl clutching a doll, her eyes as lifeless as a frozen lake."],["Shawnee","You are..."],["Leopold","Ada, I told you to let me handle this first..."],["Ada","You said you'd secure more concessions from the DL for me, but all you've done is say no."],["Ada","This is my affair. I should be the one to handle it."],["","From any angle, she looks harmless—a girl who should still be growing up under an adult's protection."],["","Yet from the moment she speaks, her voice—cold and utterly unchallengeable—takes control of the room."],["Shawnee","Ada... You're that Ada?"],["Ada","...Correct."],["Shawnee","...I need to make sure of something first..."],["Ada","Tch... What are you so worried about? You didn't hesitate when you were arguing with him."],["","Ada frowns, her gaze rebuking Shawnee for her hesitation."],["Shawnee","I didn't know we'd be dealing with a child..."],["","Now Shawnee realizes what Leopold has been trying to hide—and hint at. The hulking man who was so forceful moments ago merely turns away in silence."],["Ada","A child...? Hah. I'm nothing like you. I know exactly what I'm doing, and I'm prepared to answer for it. Besides..."],["Ada","We're signing an agreement. This is a transaction. Don't think that makes me one of you."],["Shawnee","A deal..."],["Ada","You give me power. In return, I'll follow the DL's orders for a fixed period... just like my sister..."],["Shawnee","..."],["","Shawnee crouches until they are eye to eye, meeting Ada's gaze directly."],["","The girl's earlier bravado falters under such unexpected closeness. A trace of uncertainty enters her eyes, but she quickly hides it."],["Shawnee","I understand. I'll sign the Nova Project agreement with you on behalf of the DL."],["Ada","At least you can see reason..."],["Shawnee","But I also owe you an apology. No child should have to shoulder this responsibility."],["Ada","Heh... In the end, it's all for the DL..."],["Shawnee","You're right. For the sake of the DL, we have no choice but to approve the Nova Project. But that doesn't mean we don't regret that it has come to this."],["Shawnee","I hope you can understand that."],["Ada","..."],["","Her heartfelt apology meets only dead silence. Then the electronic lock at the entrance disengages again."],["","Shawnee straightens and looks over as two figures stride in."],["???","Sorry I'm late..."],["","The man in front sweeps his gaze across the room, then heads toward Shawnee."],["???","She agreed, right?"],["Shawnee","Yes, but what I didn't expect was..."],["Leopold","Colin! I knew you were the one who came up with this plan!"],["Colin","Of course, I wasn't exactly hiding it."],["Leopold","Yeah, you only said you could poach someone from the NDF... You never said you'd be sending a child onto the battlefield!"],["Colin","Oh! So you're Ada... I'm Colin Doyle, the man overseeing the Nova Project behind the scenes. Pleasure to meet you."],["","Colin looks at Ada and waves with a smile."],["Leopold","What do you mean..."],["Colin","Well, that proves our secrecy is even better than I thought. This is my first time meeting her too. And... Lieutenant Colonel, child or not, you still made sure she got here safely, didn't you?"],["Leopold","..."],["Matilda","Hold on, hold on. Will someone tell me what's going on? And what's the deal with this kid?"],["","In the hush that follows Colin's flippant question, the other newcomer can't help but cut in."],["Leopold","Matilda, I didn't expect you to..."],["Matilda","What do you mean, me too...? Hey! It took forever to get my leave approved so I could fly home. I was already on my way to the airport when Colin suddenly dragged me here..."],["Colin","Easy... Major Matilda is genuinely in the dark, but she'll be assisting with a later phase, so I may as well give her the short version now."],["Colin","The Oceanic Conclave recently instructed us to take in a Hyper-Aptamer who escaped from the west... Oh, you know what a Hyper-Aptamer is, right? The Valkyrie who's made a name for herself on the local front is one."],["Colin","As you can see, her name is Ada. The DL will provide further enhancements, and in exchange, she'll follow our orders to a degree..."],["Matilda","Wait, wait. You're saying... we're going to perform human augmentation on this child?"],["Colin","Uh... That's about the size of it."],["Matilda","..."],["Matilda","Colin, what makes you think I'd ever agree to that?"],["Colin","Because the plan doesn't hinge on any of you. It hinges on her."],["Ada","..."],["Colin","Ada, Leopold explained every detail of the plan to you, didn't he?"],["Ada","Enough. Whatever happens, this is my choice. I'm the only one responsible for it."],["Ada","There's no one else... so stop wasting time and spare me your worthless hypocrisy."],["Colin","That's it... Major, do you understand what I mean?"],["Matilda","Hmph. So you're saying our concern is nothing but self-indulgence? Sorry, but I'm nothing like those two..."],["Colin","Of course not."],["","Colin's voice suddenly drops, losing its earlier flippancy."],["","If sincerity itself is just another layer of disguise for him, then he's the greatest actor alive."],["Colin","Sure, I could find some idiots too dumb to ask questions—cogs who'd keep the plan moving. But they would hardly be the best choice."],["Colin","Anyone can see it: if Blair made it out of the Milthus explosion alive, the NDF will never stop preparing for war. The moment they think they have even a sliver of a chance, they'll tear up the agreement without hesitation."],["Colin","So we have to enter this arms race. Tiphys can hold the line in public, but how should I put it...? His image is a little too clean. There are fights in the shadows he can never be allowed to handle. That's why the Oceanic Conclave chose me."],["Leopold","So you twist the truth in the name of peace? Colin, you..."],["Colin","No, no, I've never thought of it that way. But wherever there's light, there's shadow. Everyone here knows what kind of world this is as well as I do..."],["Colin","Especially you, Leopold. The caution and bluster a flawless command demands, and the sacrifices hidden behind it... You understand them better than anyone."],["Leopold","Hmph..."],["Shawnee","So, Rear Admiral Tiphys doesn't know about this..."],["Colin","He'll know once everything is in place. For now... it's too soon. He's the perfect soldier. The political arena beyond the battlefield is a cesspit, and it doesn't suit him."],["Colin","That's why I chose you as our official spokesperson... Shawnee, you climbed your way up from the bottom. You know exactly how to keep this plan moving through the competing power blocs without leaning on the Oceanic Conclave."],["Shawnee","..."],["Shawnee","I told you: if it can preserve the peace, I'll help... I just never expected the subject to be a child..."],["Matilda","I get it now... This is the same sweet talk you used to rope them in, isn't it...?"],["Matilda","Alright, Brigadier Colin. What line have you prepared for me this time?"],["Colin","You? Heh-heh, Matilda. I heard you were flying home for leave today, so I grabbed you on the way."],["Matilda","What? You..."],["Colin","The fewer people who know about this plan, the better. I don't want her identity exposed too soon—there would be too many variables beyond our control."],["Matilda","What the hell? You're making me sound disposable."],["Colin","Of course, there's another simple reason... You're smart, and you're a good person. You know which choice is right."],["Matilda","..."],["Colin","But people on this island commit unforgivable crimes for the sake of doing what's right all the time..."],["Colin","That's why I'm putting the plan in all your hands: one more failsafe to keep us from repeating the NDF's mistakes... I believe you can do it."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Such astonishing naivety..."],["","Ada, watching coldly from the sidelines, murmurs to herself."],["Matilda","Fine. Let's say I'm buying your crap too. But why drag me in when I'm about to leave...?"],["Matilda","I get it. Those two are too close to Ada to serve as training targets, right?"],["Colin","Exactly. First, we'll conduct the scheduled experiment on Ada, and you'll all witness it... Trust me, compared with what the NDF has done, this is nothing."],["Colin","Then comes a live combat test against an experimental ST captured from the NDF. We'll use similar new technology to run it autonomously, and you'll be in command."],["Colin","Whether it works better in a person or an ST... The higher-ups want this test to settle the question."],["Matilda","So I'm just here to play sparring partner... Fine."],["Matilda","Kid, you talk big. If you can't hold out, call it quits early, alright?"],["Ada","..."],["Ada","I won't lose."]],"561301301":[["","<yellow>...</yellow>"],["","<yellow>Ada, we'll make the perfect team...</yellow>"],["","<yellow>Don't pretend you can't see me. Don't pretend you can't hear me.</yellow>"],["","<yellow>...</yellow>"],["","<yellow>Without me, you'll lose.</yellow>"],["Ada","No!!! I haven't..."],["Colin","Haven't what?"],["Ada","Lost..."],["","The bed frame creaks beneath Ada's ragged breathing. Her eyes snap open, unfocused as she looks to the side. Her small chest rises and falls in frantic gasps, sweat-soaked hair clinging to her deathly pale cheeks like a web binding a frightened beast."],["","The reek of disinfectant and rusted metal floods her nose—no sunlight, no windows, only the emergency light humming overhead and the unreadable smile forever playing at the one-eyed man's lips."],["Colin","Bad dream? You can tell me. I won't breathe a word to anyone else..."],["Ada","..."],["Colin","Well... When it comes to keeping things close to your chest, you're more of an adult than those three outside."],["Colin","Still, I don't have many talents, but reading people is one of them... You're worried about the test results, aren't you?"],["Ada","...!"],["Colin","Relax. I know the NDF's standards, and your performance has erased every doubt about the Nova Project."],["Colin","Ada, we'll give you everything you want."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Really...?"],["","Ada's white knuckles leave crescent creases in the coarse blanket. Her fingers only now begin to uncurl, trembling like a bowstring just released. She lifts her head to look at Colin."],["Ada","Then what do you want from me? What do you want me to do?"],["Ada","Let me make one thing clear. My sister may have let those Epiphyllum girls bind her, but I will never obey your every command..."],["Colin","Easy... We've already done what we set out to do, and it went very well."],["Ada","What...?"],["Colin","The automated Computing Device implanted in your brain is built from Arashi material. It's called the PAMS System—a new DL technology designed to counter the Nova-Frame. How should I put it...? Think of it as a pilot-assist system."],["Ada","If it's only pilot assistance, how could it do all that...?"],["Colin","Of course. Yours is a custom model."],["Colin","Given a Hyper-Aptamer's tolerance, our first idea was to pack it with every scrap of combat data the DL has collected. Elise and her people objected."],["Colin","They didn't know, and wouldn't believe, that people like you and Rosa exist. But even in a simulation, what effect would implanting such a system have on a living being's consciousness?"],["Colin","Never mind a child like you. Even a battle-hardened veteran, faced with combat experience built upon tens of thousands of corpses... would have their consciousness erased and overwritten by that ocean of data, reduced to a puppet that knows only how to fight."],["Ada","..."],["Colin","Ha-ha... Relax. We ultimately proved that plan unworkable. Just treat it as a ghost story, alright?"],["Ada","No... That's not it..."],["Colin","In the end, we implanted a device with no preloaded combat data at all."],["Colin","In other words, what now exists in your mind is nothing but a blank template. As you pilot the Nova-Frame, it will gradually grow and take shape, developing the abilities you desire and becoming the form you <yellow>accept as your own</yellow>."],["Colin","As I thought, I'd rather trust a Hyper-Aptamer's ability to evolve than create a monster..."],["Ada","Can you still implement the original plan?"],["Colin","...What?"],["","Ada stares straight at Colin, eyes blazing."],["Ada","You promised to make me the strongest... If you used the original plan, I wouldn't still be like this."],["Colin","Hey, were you listening to a word I just said?"],["Colin","Injecting the combat data of tens of thousands of people directly into your brain... It's too much for a child like you..."],["Ada","You didn't know how old I was before you saw me, did you?"],["Colin","..."],["Ada","And now you use my age as an excuse... Hmph. Imposing your own standards on the subject before you—such a typically adult tactic."],["Ada","Whether I can withstand the data load is mine to decide."],["Colin","...Sigh."],["","Ada's words cut like blades. Colin lets out a short laugh, then rises."],["","The earlier warmth vanishes. He still smiles, but the scrutiny in his lone eye is now impossible to miss."],["Colin","Ada, you don't trust me... No. You don't trust anyone in the DL, do you?"],["Ada","No one on this island is worth trusting but my sister."],["Colin","But you know an agreement cannot exist without trust."],["Ada","An agreement enforced by violence and threats doesn't need trust."],["Colin","No. The aggressor trusts that the victim won't resist, while the victim trusts that the aggressor will stop there. Twisted as that certainty and hope may be, they still amount to a kind of trust."],["Colin","And from the moment I met you, I could feel it... You trust nothing beyond your own family. No agreement can stand on that..."],["Ada","Enough. You're the ones who hid the truth, and now you lecture me about trust? Laughable."],["Colin","Exactly. Saying what we don't mean is an adult habit a child like you cannot understand."],["","Ignoring Ada's scorn, Colin turns and walks toward the lounge door."],["Colin","I won't let a genius destroy herself—especially now that I've learned she's only a child..."],["Ada","...What do you know about me?!"],["","At last, Ada cries out with a protest befitting her age, stopping Colin in his tracks."],["Ada","I... I don't have that much time. My sister is still..."],["Colin","Of course I don't understand. On this island... no, in this entire world, there probably isn't anyone who could truly understand what you're going through, is there?"],["","Colin doesn't look back. His hand rests on the doorknob."],["Colin","But understand this: children aren't the only ones allowed to be willful. Adults like me get that privilege too."],["Colin","It isn't time for you and your sister to reunite yet. And it certainly isn't... time for you to destroy yourself."],["Colin","So I'll do everything in my power to keep either from happening."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","I don't believe you... If that's true, what do you want from me? Or... what do you want me to do?"],["Colin","I've already told you. I only need you to be yourself. As for why..."],["Colin","You'll understand in the end."],["Leopold","..."],["Shawnee","..."],["","Outside the lounge, the two stare at each other in silence for a while."],["","Both hold senior positions in the DL, but before Colin called them here, they were virtually strangers."],["","Their differences in position and identity create a faint barrier between them—and fuel their initial argument."],["Matilda","What are you two doing hanging around the door?"],["","The sharp click of military boots cuts through the corridor's silence. A third person, unaware of the situation, finally arrives and breaks the stalemate."],["Shawnee","To avoid putting unnecessary pressure on Ada just after she woke, Colin is speaking to her alone first."],["Matilda","Huh? Is that really a good idea? Who knows what Colin will say to her..."],["","Matilda steps up to the door and presses an ear against it."],["Matilda","Pretty good soundproofing. I can't hear a thing in there."],["Leopold","It was an order."],["","Leopold shrugs and adds helplessly."],["Matilda","An order? He rarely puts things so bluntly. He must be hiding something..."],["Leopold","No need to worry. I installed a recorder inside beforehand. We can review their conversation later."],["Matilda","Not bad... I'd heard you were capable, but I still have to admire it. How many people have been fooled by that big, dumb brute look of yours?"],["Leopold","Heh, I'll take it as a compliment."],["","The two soldiers exchange a smile, sharing an unspoken understanding."],["Shawnee","Are you... worried Colin might try something?"],["Matilda","Worried about what Colin might do? The question isn't \"whether\" he'll do something. I guarantee he will."],["Matilda","As for uncovering his real objective... most of the time, we only catch a glimpse once he's already achieved it."],["","Matilda smiles and places one hand on Shawnee's shoulder, the other on Leopold's."],["","With that gesture, the faint barrier between them begins to crumble."],["Matilda","How about we make one thing clear?"],["Matilda","You two seem to have had an unpleasant argument before I arrived. But now it's clear you both care about Ada, so... that should put us on the same side."],["Shawnee","I..."],["Leopold","I'm sorry."],["","Leopold beats Shawnee to it and offers a frank apology."],["Leopold","At first, I wanted to test the waters between you and Colin. But judging by your reactions now... I was worried for nothing."],["Shawnee","..."],["Shawnee","I was only appointed head of security at the end of last month. Most of my dealings with the military have been through Rear Admiral Tiphys's liaison, and they've mostly been about..."],["Matilda","I think I understand. Just as Colin said, you're the one operating out in the open..."],["Shawnee","Then I'd like to hear more about the other side you mentioned... about Colin."],["","Shawnee cuts Matilda off."],["","Something about her has changed since the conversation began, as though she's made up her mind."],["Leopold","There's an organization within the DL..."],["Matilda","Just as I thought. If we're going to talk about Colin, this is where we have to start."],["Leopold","War isn't fought only in open clashes at the front. Behind enemy lines, there are spies, scouts, intelligence couriers... even assassins. This organization operates where the official record ends, with Colin at the helm."],["Shawnee","...The Oversight Committee?"],["Matilda","The Oversight Committee...? Now I remember. It handled that kind of work in the early days, but it wasn't long before its counterpart, the GSA, had infiltrated it so thoroughly that it was left in tatters."],["Leopold","The Oversight Committee is still an official, public-facing institution. But as you've probably noticed, you barely hear its name anywhere on East Milkhama Island these days."],["Leopold","In a sense, when the Oceanic Conclave transferred Colin here, he took over the Oversight Committee's former role."],["Shawnee","No... If he replaced the Oversight Committee, I should have heard of Colin's organization..."],["Shawnee","What's its official name? Without a formal designation recognized by other agencies, how could it carry out any of this work?"],["Leopold","..."],["","Leopold's expression grows more solemn at Shawnee's perfectly reasonable question. His silence alone reveals how much weight it carries."],["Leopold","I don't know."],["Shawnee","...What?"],["Matilda","That's right. Everything Leopold just said was only his \"inference.\""],["Shawnee","Just... an inference?"],["","Shawnee is baffled, and that confusion begins to sour into irritation."],["","These two judge her from on high as her seniors, yet now all they can offer in explanation is guesswork. And they think she's the childish one?"],["Leopold","My \"inference\" has a basis. During the war, I served Colin's \"organization.\""],["Shawnee","You mean... you served an \"organization\" without even knowing its name?"],["Shawnee","But according to the records I have, Colin was your commanding officer, yes, but you spent the war on the front with the..."],["Leopold","All of my military operations are on record. I hardly look like a member of some covert organization, do I?"],["Shawnee","...Correct."],["Matilda","That's what makes Colin so frightening. The organization never truly existed... Or rather, people like Leopold, who even realized they were part of it, were vanishingly rare."],["Shawnee","..."],["Leopold","On several occasions, Colin sent me out on some routine assignment. Every time, something unexpected turned up: a stray enemy black-ops unit, vital supplies ripe for seizure, a turncoat exposed..."],["Leopold","Once is luck. After enough times, you begin to feel an unseen hand nudging every supposed coincidence into place."],["Leopold","Those coincidences aren't always kind. Sometimes that hand leads you straight into an enemy encirclement, where you fight for your life without knowing you're buying someone else the chance to attack or withdraw."],["Leopold","And afterward, if you work backward from the outcome, you find it wasn't only your unit. Countless teams and individuals encountered just the right coincidences to make that result possible..."],["Shawnee","...And all of it points to Colin?"],["Leopold","I once confronted Colin in private with my suspicions. He didn't deny any of it. He only said..."],["Colin","...Huh? Of course it wasn't all my doing. It's just..."],["Colin","Everyone was simply doing what they were supposed to do, right?"],["Leopold","It may have been the best solution after our intelligence division was compromised. Even the GSA couldn't discern his true objective from a web of seemingly unrelated instructions."],["Leopold","It's like a line of dominoes stretching beyond sight. No one can look at the first tile and guess where the last will fall."],["Matilda","Now you understand. The organization has no name because it doesn't exist. Or rather, Colin alone is the organization, and everyone else in the DL is one of his unwitting field operatives."],["Matilda","Of course, I haven't experienced it firsthand like Leopold. In my position, I've only heard the occasional rumor... This transfer back to the mainland also comes with orders to investigate Colin without attracting his attention."],["Matilda","I understand the results-above-all mindset, especially in wartime. But steering everyone toward a predetermined ending without their knowledge... isn't that going too far?"],["Leopold","No. Sacrificing people while keeping them completely in the dark—that's war itself. I can't accept it."],["","With that, Leopold turns to Shawnee and snaps a salute. The sharp click of his heels echoes down the corridor."],["Leopold","Shawnee, I understand your desire to preserve peace. But this plan is only a stopgap. We have to find another way."],["Leopold","The \"war\" is over. We have no reason to let it continue... least of all for that girl."],["Shawnee","..."],["Shawnee","I understand..."],["","Shawnee sighs. Matilda grins and thumps Leopold in the chest, commending the big man's unexpected eloquence."],["","Even Leopold's lips curl into the faintest smile. Finding kindred spirits here is no easy thing."],["","In a sense, people like them are the true outsiders in the DL."],["Matilda","Not bad... I'm being transferred back to the mainland tomorrow. I'll keep gathering intelligence on Hyper-Aptamers there, but I'm counting on you two to handle things here."],["Leopold","Like the NDF's Valkyrie, Colin's ultimate goal is probably to find a way to control Ada completely and force her into the DL's service."],["Leopold","I'm Ada's designated liaison within the DL. The plan will give me plenty of chances to interact with her... Now that I know Colin's objective, I'll do everything I can to keep her from that fate."],["Leopold","In the worst case, they may use technology to forcibly turn Ada into a puppet. If that happens, I'll get her off Milkhama, no matter how fiercely she resists."],["Matilda","Get her off Milkhama? Ada doesn't exactly look easy to handle. Will she go along with it?"],["Leopold","Don't worry. I'm better with children than you might think."],["Matilda","Sounds reliable... Anyway, if Colin makes any move against Ada, we stop him."],["Shawnee","...I have one question."],["","At last, Shawnee brings the one subject all three have been avoiding into the open."],["Shawnee","If Colin is truly as you describe him, then the three of us working together now must also be part of his plan... No..."],["Shawnee","In fact, this is exactly what he told us to do before the test..."],["","The lounge door suddenly swings open, and the mastermind—who sees no reason to conceal himself—appears before the three."],["","Caught off guard by the scene, Colin looks from one face to the next in surprise."],["Colin","Oh, you're all here. Saves me the trouble of telling you one by one."],["Colin","A very sudden order just came in. I'll be transferred back to the mainland before long, so we'll need someone else to take over the Nova Project."],["Colin","Leopold, Shawnee—you two should spend some time getting to know Ada. She'll be in your care from here on out."]],"561302101":[["","March 9, XC 119—Central Mines—DL Operations Command Center"],["","In the wake of the massive explosion, the entire command center descends into a state of efficient chaos. Officers who usually sit ramrod straight race back and forth, shouting as they relay and analyze the flood of intelligence pouring in from the front."],["","Amid the uproar, two uninvited guests sit in a corner, silently studying the heart of the DL."],["","At Matilda's order, the analysts and officers rushing past deliberately give them a wide berth. Even so, they can't help stealing curious glances and speculating about who they are."],["","A handful of veteran officers recognize the one-eyed man, and the sight only deepens their unease amid the current turmoil."],["","They can think of only one reason the DL would bring him back to Milkhama: the war yet to come."],["","And yet they can't help wondering whether things might be different now if he'd returned sooner."],["???","Judging by the reflexive reactions—and ignoring the merely curious—I'd say all of six people recognize you, old man."],["???","Heh. A great hero to rival Tiphys, mobbed by fans the moment you arrive... Sure. Looks like the only ones who recognize you are the poor bastards from those postwar support meetings."],["Colin","Well, what can I say? I tend to keep a low profile."],["Colin","Still... Zoey, you don't have to stay on guard every second. Why don't you find somewhere to sit? You must be tired after eight or nine hours on a plane."],["","Colin lounges back in his chair, one foot propped on the railing before him and his lone eye half-closed, utterly indifferent to the tension around him."],["","The woman he calls Zoey leans against the wall nearby, surveying everyone with cold-eyed contempt."],["Zoey","We never needed to come to these people. They can't even keep their own house in order. What help could they possibly offer us?"],["Colin","It's not like we knew that before we came..."],["Zoey","Bullshit. You'd already guessed it on the plane."],["Zoey","\"Everyone's gathered in the Central Mines...? Did no one consider that if one side thinks it's finished, they might get desperate and blow the whole lot sky-high?\""],["Colin","Mimicking an old man like me is a little mean-spirited... Besides, it was only a hunch. How was I supposed to know someone would actually be stupid enough to do it?"],["Colin","For now, let's rest here. Once Matilda's meeting wraps up, she can brief me on the island's current situation..."],["","A cold flash cuts off Colin's lazy drawl. Somehow, Zoey's knife is already darting toward his throat—but his hand locks around her wrist before it lands."],["","Colin's half-lidded eye opens a fraction. He smiles at Zoey and knocks her hand aside."],["Zoey","Hmph... You tell me to lower my guard, but have you managed it for even one second?"],["Colin","Call it an old man's occupational hazard. I wouldn't want a youngster like you catching it."],["Zoey","Hmph..."],["","Fuming at her failed strike, Zoey gives the knife an angry twirl and tucks it back into her belt."],["","This is no test. Zoey genuinely means to kill Colin."],["Colin","There are a hundred ways to kill me. Stop fiddling with these petty tricks and start learning to plan properly..."],["Zoey","Enough! I've got neither the time nor the patience for another lecture!"],["Zoey","While you sit here waiting for another pack of useless idiots to help, the Oceanic Conclave has completely lost track of the Reversion Squad's execution devices!"],["","Zoey hurls a tablet at Colin's face. This time he fails to catch it and yelps when it hits."],["","Colin picks up the tablet. Its screen continues to flicker as it searches for signals that should still be broadcasting across the island—and finds nothing."],["Zoey","Ada must have used the Nova-Frame to amplify her Hyper-Aptamer abilities and shut down the devices' remote-control systems at a distance."],["Colin","Hmm... A chance to disable the devices like that doesn't come often. She chose her moment well."],["Zoey","Let me head to the signal's last transmission point now. There's still a chance to pick up their trail and complete the Conclave's mission."],["Zoey","Wait any longer and, with Milkhama Island in this state, they'll have no trouble erasing the last traces. After that, any search will be pointless."],["Colin","No rush..."],["Zoey","Or do you trust these DL deadweights more than me? They deployed every major unit they had and still couldn't even control the situation!"],["","Zoey makes no effort to lower her voice, drawing sidelong looks from the soldiers nearby."],["","Her words cut like a merciless blade, driven straight into the DL's rawest wound. With no answer to give, the soldiers lower their heads."],["","But there's still one person here who can fight back."],["Matilda","If you really are here on the Conclave's orders..."],["Zoey","Yes?"],["","Zoey looks up with interest at Matilda striding toward them."],["Matilda","Instead of standing around making snide remarks and getting in the DL's way, why don't you go check on the Security Maintenance Force?"],["Zoey","So you're Matilda? Not bad. I suppose you're..."],["Matilda","I'm talking to Colin."],["Zoey","..."],["Colin","Hey, hey! Easy! Both of you, calm down!"],["","Colin springs out of his chair and grabs both half-raised pistols, forcing them down as he shouts."],["Zoey","I take it back... You're just a convenient pawn they dragged in to plug a hole, yet you actually think you're somebody."],["Matilda","With Milkhama the way it is, nobody would bat an eye if Vesper troops suddenly stormed in and caused a few \"accidental\" casualties, would they?"],["Colin","Matilda, meet Zoey—a violent maniac who spends every waking moment thinking about killing me. I guess that makes her my... sidekick now?"],["Zoey","So you know what Milkhama's like... Heh. Then why play the obedient little officer? This is the perfect chance to act first and ask permission later, isn't it?"],["Zoey","The truth you want exposed, the target you want erased... Keep worrying about the consequences instead of acting, and you'll be too late."],["Matilda","Funny. That's exactly what I'm planning to do."],["Colin","Zoey, one more reminder: the Conclave appointed Matilda frontline commander too. Don't take this too far!"],["Zoey","..."],["","At the mention of the Conclave's orders, most of the hostility dissipates from the room."],["","Zoey mutters a few complaints and holsters her gun first. Matilda remains wary, but she backs down as well."],["Colin","Uh... Is it too late to say \"long time no see\"?"],["Colin","Zoey doesn't mean anything by it. On our old missions, we always let her open with a little intimidation... But we all know each other here, so..."],["Matilda","Cut the crap. What did the Conclave send you back here to do?"],["Colin","Hmm... It shouldn't be hard for you to guess."],["Matilda","The Reversion Squad... No... Don't tell me..."],["Matilda","You're here for Ada?"],["Colin","That's right. A few days ago, Councilor Lukmund filed a report and Agent Veronica investigated. The Conclave now suspects Ada's Reversion Squad of betraying the DL."],["Colin","Zoey and I came to speak with Ada and find out what's really going on..."],["Matilda","..."],["","Matilda locks eyes with Colin, searching them for more information, but finds nothing."],["","Her current position leaves her no choice but to answer... Yet just as before, when everyone follows the path laid before them, everything falls neatly into someone else's plan."],["","It's time to honor the promise they hastily made in that corridor years ago."],["Matilda","I haven't received any word. The Reversion Squad answers directly to the Oceanic Conclave and isn't part of the military chain of command."],["Colin","Hmm... That's only natural. They haven't directly engaged the DLAF yet either..."],["Zoey","I knew the intel here would be useless... Fine. How many people can you mobilize? I'll take command. Begin searching the following sectors immediately..."],["Matilda","I'm afraid you'll be disappointed. Every unit is deployed to contain the unrest after the explosion. We can't spare anyone to support your operation."],["","Colin reaches out to restrain Zoey before she can erupt, then continues with a smile."],["Colin","We don't need to pull in personnel from the field. You only need to help us guard one person of interest. Surely you can manage that?"],["Matilda","A person of interest?"],["Colin","Sapientia Cognitionis, the Reversion Squad's mechanic. She's currently confined inside the ST outside."],["Colin","According to Veronica's report, Obsidian coerced her into helping orchestrate several incidents. She's cut contact now, but some details still need verification..."],["Colin","So we brought her back to Milkhama. There are a few things we need to cross-check with Ada."],["Matilda","...Not a problem."],["","Ada's status may still be uncertain, but the Conclave considers Sapientia a traitor beyond dispute. Matilda has no grounds to refuse."],["","That reluctant agreement sets the plan in motion."],["Colin","Your word alone makes this trip worthwhile."],["","Colin says it with obvious relief, then taps at his tablet and switches to another search mode. A fast-moving point of light appears on the screen."],["Colin","Right on time..."],["Zoey","That signal... No, no way. What kind of idiot walks straight into a trap?"],["Colin","If Leopold were in command, this would be much more troublesome. But the Reversion Squad as it stands has no need for elaborate tricks..."],["Matilda","What are you saying...?"],["Colin","Brace yourself, Major Matilda."],["Colin","Don't let that Nova blind you."]],"561302301":[["Zoey","Let! Me! Go!!!"],["Colin","Ow... Easy, easy, easy! I'm begging you, slow down!"],["Matilda","..."],["","The battle is over. After barking out orders for her subordinates to clear the field, Matilda returns to HQ—only to walk straight into another mess."],["","Colin clings to Zoey's gear while she muscles her way toward the ST hangar, dragging him along behind her."],["","Judging by the scene, this tug-of-war has been going on since the moment Ada appeared."],["Zoey","..."],["Zoey","Forget it. It's too late to catch her now."],["","Once Matilda appears, Zoey—perhaps suddenly embarrassed—finally admits defeat."],["","Pretending not to care, she steps aside and watches the soldiers coming and going with a cold stare."],["","After that sudden clash with the Super Pilot, an unmistakable gloom hangs over every face."],["Colin","Major Matilda, we followed your orders to the letter—we didn't interfere with the attempt to stop Ada!"],["","Colin gives Matilda a salute dripping with sarcasm."],["Zoey","Hmph... If we'd ambushed her while her ST was missing an arm, we could've taken her down..."],["Matilda","You haven't been on Milkhama Island long, so you wouldn't know. A Hyper-Aptamer like Ada can trigger her ST's self-repair at any time."],["Colin","I told her that, but she wouldn't listen. If we'd joined in, Ada wouldn't have gone so easy on them. But..."],["Colin","Major Matilda, you didn't seem particularly invested in that fight either, did you?"],["","Colin's pale violet eye narrows as he studies Matilda. His smile remains, but it feels cold and impossibly distant."],["","Matilda notices, and goosebumps rise across her skin. His expression reminds her of someone studying an insect specimen beneath a microscope."],["","She forces herself to remain calm, knowing her effort is no more convincing than a child trying to lie under an adult's questioning."],["Matilda","I don't know what you're implying. The battle broke out without warning, and the soldiers on-site did everything they could against that Super Pilot..."],["Colin","Of course. You could review the combat footage and find a plausible excuse for every command error... But is this really the level of skill expected from someone promoted to major ahead of schedule?"],["Matilda","If you have a problem with me, spare me the speech. Have the Conclave strip me of this title... I'd welcome it."],["Colin","No, no. You're the best possible choice for frontline commander..."],["Colin","For both sides."],["Matilda","..."],["Matilda","Is this what Leopold meant by a \"coincidence\"...?"],["","Matilda murmurs under her breath."],["","A sudden unease grips her, drowning her in a bone-deep chill."],["","Colin's gaze triggers it, but its true source lies in everything she's endured over the years. It all becomes a line of dominoes, toppling one after another—until it crushes her beneath its weight."],["","This isn't merely a feeling. It's happening for real."],["Colin","Ask me anything. I'm not carrying a recording device, and the Conclave will never hear a word of this."],["Zoey","How pathetic..."],["","Zoey seems to know what's coming. She turns away and fixes her attention elsewhere."],["Matilda","My transfer to the mainland after the war, and my return to Milkhama... Was that all arranged by the Conclave...? No—by you?"],["Colin","Well... Major Matilda, you applied for that opportunity to serve as an ST warfare instructor on the mainland yourself, didn't you?"],["Matilda","..."],["Colin","And your recent vacation to Milkhama had even less to do with me... Or..."],["Colin","Vacation or not, you seem to have met privately with your former superior, Rear Admiral Tiphys, quite often. Perhaps leaving Milkhama Island was never your idea in the first place?"],["Matilda","How much do you know?"],["Colin","Nothing. It's your life. You should understand it better than anyone."],["Matilda","..."],["Colin","Like everyone else, you seem to harbor some misplaced expectations of me. But... none of your choices have anything to do with me."],["Colin","Everyone was simply doing what they were supposed to do, right?"],["Matilda","No... This isn't what I wanted..."],["","Sometimes, someone like Colin makes the best confidant."],["","At least... after hearing your confession, he can't possibly know any more than he already did."],["Matilda","War, in any form... I never want to be part of it again."],["Colin","I see... Strictly speaking, you aren't part of the current DLAF command on Milkhama Island. You could refuse this appointment and return to some comfortable desk job on the mainland."],["Matilda","Then tell me: if your \"best commander\" runs away, who takes the post? You?"],["Colin","That would be a problem... It certainly won't be me. I turned Tiphys down when he offered me the job years ago."],["Matilda","Tiphys also... No. Forget the past. Given the situation now, if I leave, Lukmund takes command..."],["Colin","He won't."],["","Colin rejects Matilda's assumption without hesitation. He rarely offers anything so definite; even Zoey glances over."],["Colin","That man will never sit in this chair... So? Now that you know, will you leave?"],["Matilda","I..."],["","Matilda stares at him in surprise, but quickly regains her composure."],["","Perhaps Colin's answer is what finally lets her see the situation for what it is."],["Matilda","I still can't do it... Damn it, what is this feeling? A responsibility, or a curse?"],["Colin","Looks like I accidentally helped someone work through a few issues... So, in return, will you tell me why you let Ada escape?"],["Colin","If we could keep Ada and the Reversion Squad here, their strength would give the DL an overwhelming advantage in this unrest... Peace could come in the blink of an eye."],["Matilda","Ada has to understand that. She saved my life when we were kids... Yet she still chose to betray us. Have you ever wondered why?"],["Colin","..."],["","Of course Colin understands. Better than anyone, he knows where this story began and where it's headed."],["Matilda","I couldn't have kept her here... I'm simply grateful that all I have to do is fulfill my duty."],["Matilda","That I don't have to make the same painful choice she did."],["","The moment Colin's smile stiffens, Matilda feels a sudden sense of relief. She turns away, finally leaving this menace behind."],["Matilda","Besides, we don't need to force Ada to stay. We can win peace with our own strength."],["Matilda","That's what it means to be the \"best commander,\" isn't it?"]],"561391101":[["","<yellow>...</yellow>"],["","<yellow>...</yellow>"],["","<yellow>................</yellow>"],["","<yellow>Ada.</yellow>"],["","<yellow>So that's what strength means, then? Betrayal?</yellow>"],["Ada","Shut up."],["","In a hidden military bunker, Hasteraze slowly comes to a stop. As the cockpit pops open, Ada drops down from the ST with practiced ease."],["","Having just fought her way out of DL headquarters alone, she still looks completely unbothered—just a faint bead of sweat at her hairline gives it away."],["","As she arrives, several figures step out of the shadows."],["Ada","Everyone okay?"],["Leopold","The DL pursuers have all been split off and intercepted—thanks to those wartime shelters Sloth's got mapped out in his head. Without a way to track our frameworks, they won't be finding this place anytime soon..."],["Sloth","There are tons of unreported tunnels dug around here from the war. I used to run through them all the time."],["Paloma","Sapi's looking great too! Guess the council's been feeding her well..."],["Paloma","And here's the thing—when we first tried to contact her in secret, we got nothing. Turns out she'd just been cooped up in an ST for so long she dozed off."],["Sapientia","That's not... um... okay, fine, I did sleep a little..."],["Ada","...Sapi, they didn't do anything to you back home, did they?"],["Sapientia","Do anything... With Veronica vouching for me, and after they actually found some leftover Obsidian control hardware on me, nobody really pressed me on it."],["Ada","Nobody really pressed you on it?"],["Sapientia","Yeah, they barely even restricted my movement. I was free to go out the very next day."],["Sapientia","When I asked the officer in charge—Colin—he said he'd send me back to Milkhama to rejoin the captain when the time was right... Guess there was some jet lag involved, because I dozed off on the flight back, and by the time I woke up..."],["Ada","How could this happen..."],["","Catching everyone's expressions, Sapientia grows more and more confused."],["Sapientia","What... happened?"],["Paloma","You're kidding. So what was the point of this whole raid on headquarters, then..."],["Sloth","So we got played by Colin, completely... Thinking back on it, glad I never had to work under him during my service."],["Sapientia","What... what actually happened here?"],["","The more out of the loop someone is, the more anxious they get—Sapientia's eyes are already welling up."],["Ada","What we heard was that you'd been branded a traitor by the council and could get killed by the execution device any moment, so we launched the raid on headquarters to get you out..."],["Leopold","Ada, you don't need to blame yourself for this. Colin just poured a little fuel on something that was already coming anyway."],["Sapientia","Something that was already coming... Wait, does that mean the captain already knew about Rosa?"],["Ada","My sister's treatment is finished. I've handed her off to the GKD crew—they'll keep her safe."],["Sapientia","That's great..."],["","Hearing about Rosa, relief washes over everyone's faces, and Sapientia can't help rubbing at her eyes."],["","In less than a day, every member of the Reversion Squad has come to genuinely respect that Valkyrie."],["Paloma","What an exhausting mission... But Captain, it's not over yet, is it?"],["Sapientia","But wasn't Rosa already—"],["Ada","Seizing and losing the Legacy, working with the Predators, abandoning the Valkyrie against orders..."],["Ada","My own recklessness dragged all of you into this mess. It's only because of how unstable Milkhama's been, and because we never went head-to-head with the DL directly, that the council hasn't come down on us yet."],["Ada","Now that Colin's back on Milkhama, that means the council's finally moving. We need to move faster too..."],["","As Ada speaks, she walks over to Sapientia and reaches out, tapping lightly at the joint of her mechanical arm."],["","An indescribable feeling passes through at the touch, and suddenly Sapientia feels her breathing come easier."],["","It's as if she'd been carrying some weight for years without ever noticing it, and now Ada's brushed it off with a single careless tap."],["Ada","Sapi, I've been sensing the device inside you this whole trip, and I've already restructured it with the Hyper-Aptamer."],["Ada","I've done the same for everyone's PAMS System. From here on, the Conclave can't use it to track you or execute you... You're all free to live however you want now..."],["Sapientia","Wait... Captain, does that mean you—"],["Ada","That's right. The Reversion Squad doesn't exist anymore."],["Ada","As for me, I'm heading to GKD to pick up my sister, and I'll find a way off Milkhama..."],["Sloth","..."],["Leopold","..."],["Paloma","I see..."],["Paloma","Guess our squad's finally hit that \"everyone chases their own dream\" phase of life..."],["Sapientia","P-Paloma, don't say stuff like that! Captain, you too—"],["Paloma","What, I'm not wrong! Hey, don't grab me like that! Captain, do something about this crybaby!"],["Ada","The Reversion Squad was only ever forced together as punishment in the first place, and the Conclave—the ones who set it up—never even bothered giving us a clear standard for when that punishment ends."],["Ada","Stay here any longer, and the only ending waiting for us is quietly vanishing on some mission... And even if I make it through to the end, I can't promise the same for everyone else..."],["Paloma","Sapi, congrats on graduating... Make the rest of your life count!"],["Sapientia","You... you promised I could come back and rejoin the squad once I got back..."],["","Even Paloma's usual antics can't cut through the heaviness hanging over the squad right now."],["","The one who's always thinking a step ahead speaks up, stopping Ada as she starts to turn away."],["Leopold","No, Ada—something about what you just said doesn't add up."],["Ada","Now's really not the time to pull the \"senior officer\" act on me..."],["Leopold","Did you really finish that Neutralization Procedure on everyone's device?"],["Ada","..."],["Sapientia","Ah... Captain, your device, I remember—"],["Paloma","At a time like this, if you're still keeping secrets, Captain, that's a pretty lousy thing to do."],["Ada","Of course it's handled. My grip on the Hyper-Aptamer is way beyond what any of you can imagine right now..."],["Leopold","Then why, during the raid on headquarters—no, during the fight with GKD—didn't you use the system's ability?"],["Ada","I..."],["","<yellow>Don't ignore me... Ada...</yellow>"],["Paloma","Oh right, since the squad's disbanded now, does that mean you don't get to boss us around anymore, Captain?"],["Paloma","Tell you what, you all hold her down and I'll take a look!"],["Ada","Fine... fine, just don't touch me... After this I'm planning to deal with the positioning function too."],["Ada","If the Oceanic Conclave's always got eyes on me, I can't exactly take my sister and leave..."],["Leopold","So what's the plan?"],["","<yellow>Yeah... Ada, what's the plan?</yellow>"],["Ada","I said—shut up!!!"],["Leopold","..."],["","As if she can't quite believe she just snapped like that, Ada's eyes go wide, a flicker of fear behind them."],["","Everyone who'd started drifting toward her stops in their tracks without meaning to."],["Ada","No... that's not... I..."],["","<yellow>It's not too late to come back to the DL...</yellow>"],["Ada","Hmm..."],["","She grips her forehead and stumbles back a couple steps, leaning against the ST's leg, breathing hard."],["","Whatever ease she had a moment ago is gone, and the exhaustion's impossible to hide now."],["Ada","Trust me, I'll shut it down with the Hyper-Aptamer..."],["Leopold","If you could've done that, you already would have."],["Ada","No... it's just, to shut down your devices I still needed it for simulations..."],["Paloma","The captain doesn't know the first thing about anything outside of combat—modifying hardware isn't something you can just psychic your way through."],["Leopold","So how exactly do you get a device to agree to shut itself down?"],["Ada","..."],["Leopold","So that wasn't just something you imagined as a kid..."],["Ada","Yeah... lately, I've been hearing it talk more and more..."],["","Like some hollow excuse at a work function, Ada's attempt to dodge the question gets seen through in an instant."],["","Once she decides to just come clean, something in her eases up—like the discomfort in her head is lighter too."],["","Maybe there was never any point hiding it in the first place."],["Leopold","Some of you might not know this yet... The device implanted in Ada's prefrontal cortex is called A-00. Unlike a standard PAMS System, it's a specialized build—more raw processing power, no pre-loaded data."],["Leopold","Colin promised me this thing would only grow the more Ada used it, shaping itself into whatever she needed... But going by what happened after, that guy was clearly lying through his teeth."],["Leopold","Works a lot like our execution protocols. The second Ada so much as thinks about defying the DL, A-00 kicks in on its own to interfere... Like it's got a will of its own, and it's waking up."],["Ada","Interfere is putting it too strongly. I can still call on it for backup even now... Maybe I really did just imagine all that."],["","<yellow>No. That's not what you actually think.</yellow>"],["Ada","Shawnee's people ran a full check on the device back then too. No signs of tampering."],["Leopold","Simple—those people got played by Colin as well. Setting that up would've been nothing for him... We just didn't clock it until after the fact."],["Sloth","No point rehashing old news. Real problem is, the captain can't fix her own device the way she fixed ours. Right?"],["Leopold","...Exactly."],["Ada","No... I can try again..."],["Paloma","Oh, Captain, don't go underestimating what that arashi stuff can do."],["Paloma","No willpower's strong enough to fight off that kind of corruption and control... Sigh, we already went through this once with Rosa. Do we really have to sit through the sequel?"],["Paloma","Still, you actually opening up about it puts you miles ahead of her back when she wouldn't budge."],["Ada","..."],["","<yellow>That's right—do you really think you can be... stronger than your sister?</yellow>"],["Ada","But I have to be..."],["Leopold","Then do what I did back then. Use the experimental Rebirth Serum and go straight to surgical removal..."],["Paloma","Don't be ridiculous. This isn't like the vice captain's—you can't just pry this thing out with your bare hands. The captain's is embedded in her prefrontal cortex! To have the slightest chance of success, you'd need a high-end research facility at the very least."],["Paloma","And have you forgotten? With the captain's physiology, if she takes the serum... she could become the strongest person in the world for a time, not just Milkhama."],["Paloma","Then, just like Rosa, the arashi particles won't be expelled normally. They'll accumulate inside her, stimulating her neurons without end until she falls into a coma... And we both know we aren't getting a second miracle like the one in the Central Mines..."],["Ada","...Then skip the serum and operate directly."],["Paloma","Huh? Then the captain wouldn't even make it to a coma. She'd probably die right there on the operating table."],["Ada","Paloma, you needn't worry. Even if it fails..."],["Paloma","No, no, no, no... This is science! You can't change the outcome with the power of belief or whatever!"],["","<yellow>If you throw your life away like this, won't your sister be heartbroken?</yellow>"],["","<yellow>Ada, the DL will accept both you and your sister. Why refuse to consider that possibility?</yellow>"],["Paloma","This plan is far too risky. If the captain wants to die, I can think of more efficient ways..."],["Sapientia","...There is one way."],["","Sapientia, silent until now, suddenly speaks and offers a way out of the deadlock."],["Sapientia","But this wouldn't alter the Neutralization Procedure itself. The captain may lose her ability to operate the device... Can you accept that?"],["Paloma","Thank goodness. Anything's better than surgery with a 95% fatality rate."],["Ada","Sapi, tell us what you have in mind."],["Sapientia","Back on the mainland, Veronica gave me access to material on implanted devices while I was researching ways to counter the execution system inside me... I found no solution, but I remember seeing information about the special A-00 model."],["Sapientia","Captain, was this model's PAMS System originally installed in Puppets as well?"],["Ada","Puppets? Don't tell me..."],["Leopold","Ada's opponent in her first test was a Puppet built with similar technology!"],["","Leopold cries out in excitement. His words match the hazy memory in Ada's mind."],["","The rest of the squad was never told about that incident, further confirming the credibility of Sapientia's information."],["Sapientia","That's right. A-00 wasn't originally developed for the captain. It was intended to replace Hyper-Aptamers as the operators of the Nova-Frame developed by the NDF."],["Sapientia","Only after learning of the captain's existence did the research team open a second line of development, erase the system's combat data, and implant it into her brain as a blank slate."],["Sapientia","Over the years, the device in the captain's brain has grown. By fighting alongside her, it has adapted to piloting Hasteraze and is now virtually identical to the device envisioned in the original plan..."],["Ada","You mean we should continue..."],["Sapientia","That's right. We can complete the experiment as it was originally conceived."],["Sapientia","If we can find another Hasteraze, tune its PAMS System, and recreate a similar operating environment... transferring the system out of the captain's brain may be possible."]],"561303101":[["Ada","..."],["","Another unfamiliar place."],["Special Trial Unit Member","Report! The ore refinery garrison has submitted a request for reinforcements. They want a squad dispatched to survey the surrounding area..."],["Special Trial Unit Commander","Of all times... Tell them to hold out a little longer."],["Special Trial Unit Member","But... this is their third request. The civilians nearby are starting to feel..."],["Special Trial Unit Commander","Escorting the councilor takes priority. Understood?!"],["Special Trial Unit Member","Understood!"],["","This appears to be a military staging area. Soldiers hurry back and forth, calling out to one another as they prepare for their next assignments."],["","No one notices her... No. They're all deliberately looking away."],["Ada","What a boring place."],["","After standing alone for more than ten minutes, Ada silently retreats to a corner and crouches down."],["","Colin told her to stay put and wait, but she can't stand all those glances sweeping over her, then darting away."],["Special Trial Unit Member A","Is that the kid?"],["Special Trial Unit Member B","Seriously...? Can she even climb into an ST?"],["","This is... a little unsettling."],["Ada","How much longer is that guy going to take...?"],["","During her time with the DL, she spends most of her days in the lab. It's the only place she knows."],["","Her routine isn't much different from life with the NDF—training and tests, day after day. But just as Colin promised, at least the pain is gone."],["","Training no longer pushes her to the brink every time. No one injects her with strange drugs, and the cries of other Hyper-Aptamers no longer fill the air while she sleeps."],["","They even arrange a few general education classes for her, finally granting her old wish to attend school... Even if she has no classmates, and the instructors and researchers are all cold and distant."],["","Now that the pain that defined her days is gone, along with the enemy she once lived to avenge herself on, something feels wrong. Somehow... she feels weaker."],["Ada","They call it socialization training... She'd rather have a few more combat drills."],["","She looks forward to training now. Only inside an ST does she feel in control of herself."],["","Otherwise, she ends up like this... Anxious just from waiting for someone in a public place..."],["","What she doesn't realize is that this is perfectly normal for an ordinary girl."],["Dean","Hey, kid. Are you lost?"],["Ada","..."],["","A young man crouches beside her. He's tall and powerfully built, but still carries the unmistakable innocence of a student."],["Dean","Where are your parents? Who brought you here?"],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Leave me alone."],["","Being ignored feels awful, but having some complete stranger strike up a conversation isn't much better."],["","It has nothing to do with what happened. Being in an unfamiliar place is simply uncomfortable."],["Dean","Well, this is awkward... How about this? I'm Dean Knight, a student trainee assigned to the Special Trial Unit. Will you tell me your name?"],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Ada. You can go now."],["","Ada rises and quickly walks off. Seeing Dean crouched in a corner to talk to a little girl is giving even her secondhand embarrassment."],["","As for where she's going... she hasn't decided. Probably another corner where she can crouch and wait."],["Dean","Ada... Oh! Are you the Super Pilot the others mentioned?"],["","Rather than grab her, Dean catches up in a few quick strides and asks with open curiosity."],["Ada","Super Pilot?"],["Dean","Yeah. I heard a Super Pilot named Ada was coming to train the unit. So that's you?"],["Ada","...Do you really think I am?"],["","Remembering the soldiers who looked down on her earlier, Ada answers with a sarcastic question... Yet for some reason, this young man feels different."],["","Sure enough, unlike everyone else who doubts her because of her age, he believes her almost instantly."],["","Or maybe his brain simply isn't wired for thought or suspicion."],["","By the time Ada snaps back to the moment, Dean has hurried in front of her and bowed deeply."],["Dean","I'm sorry, Pilot Ada!"],["Ada","...Huh?"],["Dean","I can't believe I mistook you for some lost kid hiding in a corner and anxiously peeking around for her parents. Come to think of it... you were inspecting everyone's work, weren't you?"],["Dean","You're so easy to overlook if people aren't paying attention!"],["Ada","Hey, are you trying to pick a fight...?"],["","Several nearby personnel stop what they're doing and turn to watch with interest."],["","Dean's voice is rather difficult to ignore."],["","This is suffocating."],["Dean","I'm sorry, but I'm not trying to pick a fight!"],["Dean","I just think it's admirable how you can use your physical advantages to complete a mission even outside combat, Pilot Ada! There's a lot I can learn from you!"],["Ada","No, you are trying to pick a fight..."],["Dean","In that case, may I ask you something? Would you be willing to join me on a mission?"],["Ada","No."],["Dean","But with a Super Pilot like you there to guide me, I'm sure I could... Wait, what? You don't want to?"],["Ada","That's right. It's nothing personal. I just... won't work for the DLAF."],["","Ada ignores Dean's puzzled look and coldly surveys the onlookers around them."],["","As if venting her anger at the whispers from earlier, she raises her voice."],["Ada","Armies exist to wage war, and wars are nothing but games played by the people at the top... I'm not going to become someone else's pawn like all of you!"],["Dean","Pilot Ada, you..."],["Ada","Don't look at me like that... You're not even a real soldier yet. You're just a half-trained rookie, aren't you?"],["Ada","Plenty of people here know the truth and still willingly become pawns... What about you? How long can that mindless enthusiasm of yours last?"],["Ada","Once you've seen the truth behind it all, you'll..."],["","A shrill alarm suddenly tears through the entire staging area."],["Warning","Level One alert! Level One alert! The ore refinery garrison has engaged the NDF and been completely wiped out. Special Trial Unit, prepare for immediate deployment..."],["","At the mention of the NDF, Ada's hand clenches almost instinctively."],["","That familiar target, the one so deserving of her hatred, has appeared again."]],"561303301":[["Ada","..."],["Dean","Enough with the long face... A girl your age looks better when she smiles, doesn't she?"],["Ada","Are you saying I'm not pretty enough?"],["Dean","Uh... No, that's not what I meant..."],["","Whether through luck or some last-second evasive maneuver, the cockpit escapes serious damage, as does Dean inside it."],["","Still, they can't rule out internal injuries from the impact... So despite his protests, once reinforcements arrive, Dean is carried onto the massive engineering command vehicle and laid on the medical platform."],["","Particle interference has also caused several malfunctions in Ada's ST, so she rides back in the same vehicle, watching Dean from nearby."],["","For now, he's the only person she has to talk to... And judging by this single-celled organism's behavior..."],["","<yellow>Maybe the DLAF isn't made up entirely of jerks and liars.</yellow>"],["Ada","Maybe..."],["Dean","Hmm? Pilot Ada, who are you talking to?"],["Ada","...What?"],["","Something feels off. Wasn't he the one who just asked her a question?"],["Dean","What are you talking about...? You seemed kind of strange just now..."],["Ada","I'm strange...? Hey, haven't you noticed there's something even stranger about the way you address me?"],["Dean","What seems strange about it?"],["Ada","This is a weird thing for me to ask too, but why do you keep being so formal with a little girl...? It's kind of gross."],["Dean","I... Is it?!"],["Ada","Right."],["","Dean has clearly never considered that before... If he had, he certainly would've said so."],["","He can't think entirely inside his own head. His mouth has to help with the process."],["","Talking with him makes it easy to fall into the same rhythm, blurting things out before thinking..."],["","This may be the first time she can remember simply chatting and saying whatever comes to mind."],["Dean","It's just... you're so young, Pilot Ada, yet your piloting skills are incredible. You stay calm in battle, and your ability to calculate on the fly is amazing..."],["Dean","Basically, I just can't stop admiring you."],["Ada","Uh... Most people just think I'm a monster..."],["Ada","Just like them..."],["Dean","I thought I was already one of the best my age. Guess there's always someone better..."],["Ada","Wait. How old are you?"],["Dean","Fourteen."],["Ada","...Wait! You're that tall at fourteen?!"],["Dean","People say I eat a lot, so I grow fast."],["Ada","..."],["","Ada unconsciously touches the top of her head."],["","I'm... a little jealous."],["","If only she could grow faster. Then she wouldn't need all those assistive devices in the cockpit, and the controls would be much easier to operate..."],["Ada","Guess I need to eat more... Is that the only way to catch up with my sister faster...?"],["Dean","Pilot Ada, you have a sister?"],["Ada","Yeah. She's way stronger than me."],["Dean","Stronger than you, Pilot Ada? Then... just how strong is she?"],["Ada","Heh. Stronger than that brain of yours can possibly imagine."],["Dean","I can't imagine it...? Then I'll just have to see for myself, right?"],["Dean","What unit is your sister with? I'll apply there for my next training assignment!"],["Ada","..."],["Dean","Oh, sorry. You said you aren't part of the DLAF, Pilot Ada, so your sister must not be either..."],["Ada","No. My sister is a soldier too."],["","The words leave her almost like a sigh."],["Ada","But the unit she's in... is one you'll never be able to join."],["Dean","I see. The requirements must be incredibly high... Then I'll just have to work even harder!"],["Ada","...Huh? That's not what I meant..."],["Dean","I'm still just a half-trained rookie. I'm nowhere near qualified to fight beside you, am I?"],["Dean","I need to get stronger and become... a real soldier!"],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Dean, do you remember what I said back at the base?"],["Ada","Soldiers are nothing but..."],["Dean","That's one thing I can't agree with you on, Pilot Ada!"],["Ada","Heh. You're only a student. Of course you wouldn't understand..."],["Dean","Then what about everything we did today? What does that count for?"],["Dean","Are you going to deny that we saved an entire factory district full of civilians from the NDF?"],["Ada","I can't deny the facts. But we did that, not the DLAF..."],["Dean","But without the DLAF, we wouldn't even have known it was happening! How could we have saved anyone?"],["Ada","..."],["Dean","Protecting people who can't protect themselves—that's a soldier's duty."],["","The argument between two naive youths finds its answer in the facts."],["","Ada desperately searches for a rebuttal, but only a few murmured fragments of her thoughts escape."],["Ada","B-But my sister... She..."],["Dean","I know everything you said is real, Pilot Ada. The world isn't like a cartoon where passion and guts can solve everything."],["Dean","But when I finally face the truth, I hope I can still say the same thing I did today..."],["Dean","That's what makes a real soldier!"],["","As Dean's emphatic declaration ends, the moving vehicle rolls to a stop. Several squad members hurry over and lift his stretcher."],["","Even as they carry him away, he keeps waving vigorously at Ada. The motion pulls at his wounds, leaving him grimacing in pain."],["Ada","..."],["Colin","Hey, you're back."],["Colin","I couldn't find you after I finished my business. Scared me half to death... What if you'd gotten lost?"],["Ada","Stop treating me like a kid..."],["Colin","You really are... Forget it. I came up with a dozen excuses to convince you to take a little trip with the DLAF, and then you went out on your own."],["Colin","So, how did the mission feel?"],["Ada","..."],["","Ada strides ahead, trying to leave the annoying old man behind, but Colin catches up in a few steps."],["Ada","Not great."],["Colin","Then what did you think of that Dean kid? Not bad, right?"],["Ada","...He was okay."],["Colin","Heh. Getting an \"okay\" from a Super Pilot would make his day."],["Ada","Not my problem."],["Colin","Then, Ada, let me ask you again..."],["","Ada stops midway through carefully climbing down from the overly high platform, one hand gripping the railing."],["","She knows what Colin is about to ask... Her answer needs careful thought."],["Colin","I'll give you more opportunities to take field assignments from now on. Is that all right?"],["Ada","I suppose... Simulation training alone won't prepare me for real combat..."],["Colin","An evasive answer like that isn't your style."],["Ada","..."],["","She draws a deep breath and faces the prejudice shifting within her."],["Ada","I need to understand the purpose of a mission, not merely the assignment itself."],["Ada","And whether I accept it... will be my decision."]],"561304101":[["","Building on Sapientia's hypothesis, Leopold quickly proposes a plan of action."],["Leopold","That's the plan. We split into two teams. Ada seizes the Hasteraze prototype while the rest of us secure this border laboratory and prepare to transfer the system."],["Sapientia","Hmm... No problem. If everything goes smoothly, we can begin the transfer as soon as Captain brings the other Hasteraze here."],["Paloma","Then Captain's tracking data is still in Colin's hands, right? Is that safe?"],["Sapientia","I added some anti-tracking devices to Captain's ST. They should scramble the signal for a while... probably..."],["Paloma","Wow! I never expected you to be this useful in this part of the story, Sapi!"],["Sapientia","R-Really? Ehehe..."],["Sloth","Um... Is Captain fit to handle a solo mission in her current condition?"],["Paloma","Huh? Is anyone still questioning her strength?"],["Sloth","That's not it. I just... Ada, are you really okay?"],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Don't worry about me... Your captain won't choke when it matters."],["Paloma","There it is—the Rosa-style line."],["Ada","No. I'm not the same as my sister was back then... I can feel the device's condition. For now, I can still keep it suppressed."],["Ada","As long as I don't use the device, I can remain stable."],["Leopold","No one in the DL should be strong enough to force Ada to use it right now."],["Ada","...Correct."],["Leopold","Even so, don't push yourself."],["Ada","Got it."],["Paloma","Enough, Vice Captain. This isn't the time for all that. Keep going and you'll never stop."],["","And so, the A-00 transfer plan begins."]],"561304301":[["","Just as expected, the Hasteraze prototype remains stored in this research institute. After all, no one but Ada can pilot it."],["","Several years ago, the DL built her an exact duplicate of Hasteraze for emergencies. She remembers throwing a tantrum and refusing to adapt to a new ST."],["","Then one day, they secretly swapped the two STs—and even Ada, their pilot, failed to notice any difference. Only she understands the embarrassment... The older unit is placed in storage at the institute as a reserve."],["","Ada, the undefeated Super Pilot, never imagined she'd need that old reserve unit..."],["Ada","And now it's my only chance..."],["","Ada looks back at the ST behind her through the display and sighs."],["","She is controlling it remotely through brainwaves, guiding it along behind her. The sensation enveloping her is indescribably familiar, like slipping into clothes from childhood."],["","That's why she doesn't have the others retrieve it. This is her ST, and no machine is easier for her to control."],["","<yellow>Ada, deceiving me means deceiving yourself...</yellow>"],["Ada","Shut up... You don't get a say in this."],["","Perhaps to escape Dean as quickly as possible, she uses A-00 again, and that infuriating voice resumes echoing through her mind."],["Ada","Even I couldn't tell those two STs apart, and I was their pilot... Hmph. When the time comes, you'll crawl out of my head like a good little parasite."],["","<yellow>No... because I am you...</yellow>"],["","<yellow>And as you are now... you can't defeat him...</yellow>"],["Ada","Defeat who? You're the only one left standing between my sister and me..."],["","The ST stops."],["","The person A-00 spoke of appears before Ada."],["Ada","...Dean, what are you doing?"],["Dean","..."],["","She is certain her strike destroyed Ranger's braking system. With nothing to absorb the impact, the collision should have knocked Dean unconscious inside the cockpit."],["","Even if he regained consciousness quickly, he shouldn't be able to pilot his ST or threaten her again... Or so Ada thought..."],["","Yet now, this man stands before her."],["","On the road leading out of the research institute."],["Dean","I'm here to stop you."],["","Dean raises his riot baton and points it at Ada inside the cockpit."],["","He isn't piloting his own ST."],["","Armed with nothing but flesh and blood, he stands before Hasteraze—arguably the strongest single-pilot ST in the DL arsenal."],["","Ada instinctively leans back. For once, the hand gripping her control stick feels warm and slick with sweat."],["","She's nervous."],["Ada","A-Are you insane?! Are you trying to get yourself killed?!"],["","Ada lowers the cockpit shield and shouts at Dean."],["","Without the cockpit's climate control, the hot, dust-choked air brushes her cheeks, making everything feel even more real."],["","The battle was real. Dean standing before her is real too."],["","The reality of it is almost enough to make her recoil."],["Dean","No... I did stop you, didn't I...? Cough, cough..."],["","Dean breaks into a violent coughing fit and nearly drops the baton."],["","The earlier impact may have damaged his organs, and the concussion leaves his mind swimming. Still, he keeps his eyes fixed on Ada."],["","Not once does he waver. That's Dean."],["Ada","Stop me...? No. Against an ST, you can't possibly..."],["Dean","Then you'll have to go through me!"],["Ada","...!"],["","Dean's furious challenge stops the words in Ada's throat."],["","She can only stare at him, at a loss for what to do."],["Dean","I knew it... You're incredibly strong, Pilot Ada, but you're far too kind."],["Dean","If you've truly chosen to betray the DL, don't hesitate. Go straight through me."],["Ada","Dying like this would mean nothing..."],["Dean","I'm a soldier! My orders are to hold this position to the death!"],["Ada","Th-Then why do you still believe in the DLAF?!"],["","Without her noticing, tension becomes fear—and now, anger."],["","Ada roars back at Dean."],["Ada","Right now, you're nothing but tools for those politicians, forcing the people of Milkhama down a road they can never turn back from..."],["Dean","Is that still true now?"],["Ada","...What?"],["Dean","If you know the truth and are willing to tell me, Pilot Ada, then plenty of others must know it too."],["Dean","So is the DLAF still nothing but a weapon in a power struggle? Or is it trying to protect people now?"],["","Ada thinks of Matilda. As frontline commander, she has been stalling for time, desperately searching for a way to break the deadlock and reach a peaceful end."],["Dean","I have partners I trust. Now that the truth is out, they would never help evil prevail or keep fighting a war that never should've happened."],["Dean","I trust them, and I trust myself. That's why I can trust the DLAF. And..."],["Dean","You're one of those people too, Pilot Ada."],["","Ada's gaze darts away. She can no longer look Dean in the eye."],["","Her eyes flick to a nearby mirror. The face staring back has lost its usual confidence and brightness."],["","It looks like someone else's face now—skin deathly pale, dark circles stark beneath the eyes after days of relentless pressure."],["Ada","...Maybe I used to be. But everything is different now."],["Ada","Dean, what I'm doing now isn't for the DL. It isn't about protecting the greatest number of people either..."],["Dean","I know. I can tell you've already made your choice, Pilot Ada. Deep down, I want to support you. But..."],["Ada","I don't want to be your enemy either. I just..."],["Dean","You're strong."],["Ada","...!?"],["Dean","If you've truly made your choice, then don't hesitate now. Don't run from it..."],["Dean","Otherwise, come back with me!"],["","......"],["","..."],["","................"],["","After a long pause, Hasteraze's cockpit closes again, shutting reality back outside."],["","She buries one hand in her hair. A moment later, the other releases the control stick and joins it as she bows her head."],["","A suffocating sensation has haunted her chest since moments ago, like the aftermath of a crushing blow. Her heart pounds furiously, yet it feels as though it pumps air instead of blood."],["","Pain and confusion pierce her. What weighs on her heart is something she can't understand."],["","<yellow>Did you win, Ada?</yellow>"],["Ada","I lost."],["","The admission brings relief, as if she has earned the right to breathe again. She grips the controls and turns her ST around."],["","There should be another passage leading outside."],["","One Dean isn't blocking."],["Ada","Dean... Looks like I'm the half-trained rookie."],["Ada","Even so, I won't give up."]],"561392101":[["Colin","Hmm... Yes, yes. We'll need personnel and equipment like these..."],["Colin","You can scrape all that together, can't you?"],["Ma'at","...Of course. If it's an order from the Oceanic Conclave."],["","Ma'at falls silent for a moment before forcing the words out."],["","With a single request, the Oceanic Conclave's representative requisitions nearly a third of the Security Maintenance Force's resources. Combined with the losses from the earlier pursuit of GKD, the force is now close to paralysis."],["","Yet that very proximity to collapse makes her all the more uneasy. The laid-back man before her seems to know everything, effortlessly holding the line at the brink."],["","At this rate, Lord Lukmund's plan will..."],["Colin","Well, that's a huge help. Sounds like East Island is getting along just fine."],["Colin","The military and politicians alike have been so courteous to a newcomer like me. I hardly deserve it..."],["Ma'at","You flatter me... Mr. Colin, I'll go instruct my subordinates to reallocate the supplies."],["Colin","Great. I'll leave it to you."],["","Colin gives a cheerful wave and watches Ma'at lift the flap of the temporary tent..."],["Zoey","Tsk!"],["Colin","Zo—"],["","Bang! Bang!"],["","Two gunshots punch a pair of black holes through the engineering plans hanging at the rear of the tent."],["","If Zoey hadn't lunged forward and tackled Colin, those holes would be in his chest."],["Zoey","Stay down! Assassin!"],["","After shouting the warning, Zoey shoves aside Ma'at, who seems dazed by the gunfire, and charges out of the tent."],["","She draws her pistol and scans the area, then follows the surrounding gazes to a blurred figure in the distance."],["","Bang!"],["","The figure drops at the sound of a shot."],["Colin","Whew... One more shot and he would've had me..."],["Zoey","No. One more shot and he'd still have missed."],["Colin","I could've died of fright. Assassinations are my one great weakness."],["Zoey","..."],["","The assassin's body is brought to the command room. Colin makes a tremendous fuss nearby while Zoey and Ma'at handle the actual examination."],["","Zoey pinches the corpse's face, gives it a cursory glance, then leaves Ma'at to do the rest."],["","The corpse wears a standard DLAF uniform, and identity verification confirms he is who he appears to be. Still, Ma'at's meticulous examination turns up an important clue."],["Ma'at","It seems Vesper agents have infiltrated the Security Maintenance Force."],["","Ma'at lifts the corpse's wrist and finds a faint mark on the back of his tactical wristband."],["Ma'at","They were probably looking for a chance to assassinate a councilor—or any high-ranking military figure—to sow chaos, and happened to spot Mr. Colin..."],["Colin","Oh? Do I really look like such a big shot?"],["Colin","Strange. There shouldn't be many people on this island who know me..."],["Ma'at","Perhaps they judged from my reaction. As Councilor Lukmund's aide, I've been in and out of the Peacekeeping Force quite often lately."],["Colin","Oh! That explains it. I have Councilor Lukmund to thank for my newfound fame."],["","Despite narrowly escaping death by gunfire, Colin remains as laid-back as ever."],["Colin","But if that's the case, those Vesper agents are awfully dangerous... I'll be reporting this to the council as well."],["Ma'at","My sincerest apologies. We'll tighten our control over force personnel..."],["Colin","No harm done. You've already done an excellent job! Go on and finish your work!"],["Ma'at","Alright."],["","Ma'at leaves the command room. This time, no bullets accept the tent flap's invitation inside. Only Colin, Zoey, and a corpse remain."],["Colin","What do you make of it?"],["Zoey","Don't need a second look. They're Lukmund's people."],["","It is obvious that by \"them,\" Zoey means Councilor Lukmund."],["Colin","You'll have to give me some evidence. Not that anyone on this island cares about evidence..."],["Zoey","This guy had a pinhole receiver in his ear canal. And when Ma'at lifted the curtain, I caught her hand making a signal in front of her."],["Zoey","Of course, the receiver's already been removed. Don't need to look to know that either."],["Zoey","As for the mark on his hand... only someone genuinely stupid—or pretending to be—would believe it."],["Colin","Not bad. No wonder you're the second person I've ever had high hopes for... So why'd you save me just now?"],["Zoey","Because I'm the only one allowed to kill you."],["Colin","Heh. Not bad..."],["","Colin chuckles, then turns back to studying the base's engineering plans."],["","But Zoey can't let it go."],["Zoey","Hey, what are you scheming now? Those people are trying to have you killed!"],["Colin","Make someone a target, then take them out—an assassination and frame-up this childish only proves how stupid Lukmund is. What's there to worry about?"],["Zoey","Then why use resources this risky? No..."],["Colin","We can't keep imposing on the DLAF, can we? If the two sides become too uneven, we'll have to reshuffle the deck."],["Colin","And now I have one more piece of leverage over Lukmund. I can squeeze a little more out of her secretary later..."],["Zoey","And what are you plotting with all this construction?!"],["Colin","Oh... you mean this base? I'm preparing for what's to come, of course..."],["Zoey","The council tasked us with Ada, not building fortifications out here!"],["Zoey","Now that Sapientia's been taken away, there's even less chance Ada will come to us. We should be using the time while her signal is still..."],["Colin","Exactly. She managed to whisk Sapientia away from DL headquarters before. Don't we need a stronger base if we want to hold her off?"],["Colin","She's a Super Pilot... Zoey, surprising as it may be, we're the weaker side in this mission. We're the underdogs."],["Zoey","..."],["Colin","This time, I'm going to teach you how the weak defeat the strong..."],["Zoey","Enough. I should've known better than to expect useful advice from an old man like you."],["","Zoey cuts off Colin's lecture and walks to the tent flap. As she lifts it, she continues with her back to him."],["Zoey","Like you, I found myself a helper. Together, we'll drag Ada back... You stay here. Try not to get yourself killed."],["Zoey","This time, I'll do better than you."]],"561305101":[["DL Politician","A Super Pilot, huh...? The DLAF brass finally grew a brain. They understand now: the war may be over, but peace is the more dangerous battlefield."],["DL Politician","The public needs heroes, and the opposition needs targets. A parade of grease-stained veterans on Victory Day can't provide that, nor can Tiphys, who avoids public appearances unless absolutely necessary..."],["DL Sergeant","Hahaha! Those idiots need someone who matches the hero in their heads. A Super Pilot is perfect, isn't she?"],["DL Sergeant","Young, powerful, beautiful... Yes, that's what they want. It'll drive up public support and votes even further."],["DL Wealthy Merchant","Hey, could that Super Pilot put on a demonstration in one of our company's STs? You couldn't ask for better advertising..."],["Shawnee","I believe this plan can satisfy all of your needs, but I'll need to discuss the next steps with the other parties in charge..."],["DL Politician","No problem, no problem. Just tell us what you need when the time comes. We'll make it happen."],["DL Politician","She's the DL's future superstar. Of course we need to develop her properly, right? Hahaha..."],["DL Sergeant","But... where is Ada? At a time like this, shouldn't she at least make an appearance...?"],["","After concluding the DL leadership's secret presentation, Shawnee wears her signature smile as she greets the politicians, businesspeople, and officers below the stage."],["","Amid the clinking glasses, she slips backstage and finds the person meant to be the star of the entire gathering."],["Shawnee","That segment was supposed to be your debut before the DL's senior leadership..."],["Ada","..."],["Shawnee","Did something happen?"],["Ada","If I'd known it would be like this, I wouldn't have snuck away from the unit behind Leopold's back..."],["Ada","Being under his thumb is bad enough, but seeing these people here... makes me even angrier."],["","With that, Ada turns to leave. It seems she stayed at the venue only long enough to say those words to Shawnee."],["Shawnee","Ada, this is the best opportunity we'll get... Even Leopold, who opposed it most strongly, allowed you to come with me, didn't he?"],["Ada","No. He has no idea. After getting caught twelve times, I'm finally confident I can slip past him."],["Shawnee","Really...? But before I left, he gave me this sandwich and a can of Ms. Chili."],["Shawnee","\"If you're back late, eat these to tide yourself over. She likes drinking this stuff.\""],["Ada","..."],["","Ada stares at the simple meal in Shawnee's hands and falls into an awkward silence. Then she walks back and takes the can of soda."],["","She yanks the tab open and takes a fierce gulp."],["","For Ms. Chili's sake, she gives Shawnee a few words' worth of her time."],["Shawnee","Leopold may object, but he's the best example himself... If he hadn't completely broken with the Ashford family after the war, he could've accomplished far more as their representative than he can now."],["Ada","How is that any different from what happened to my sister and me?"],["Shawnee","Valkyrie..."],["Ada","I may have struck a deal with you, but I also told you I'd only follow orders to a point..."],["Ada","My time with the DL has taught me that its politicians are every bit as hypocritical as the warmongers in the West are bloodthirsty. You always wrap your true intentions in lies."],["Ada","The people at the top reap the rewards of victory while ordinary Milkhamans lose their voice. Some are even driven from their homes, reduced to so-called vagrants with nowhere left to belong."],["Ada","I won't repeat my sister's mistakes."],["Shawnee","..."],["Shawnee","Ada, you want to become stronger, don't you?"],["Ada","Yeah. I came here to become the \"strongest,\" not for this boring..."],["Shawnee","Then let me tell you something. Training and combat aren't the only ways to grow stronger in this world. Authority is another form of strength."],["Ada","Then I don't want that kind. I'll make up for it elsewhere."],["Shawnee","The more you reject the rules of this world, the more tightly they bind you."],["Shawnee","You believe your sister chose the wrong path. But do you realize...?"],["Shawnee","Only the position she attained within the NDF allowed her to arrange your escape and bring you here."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","My sister had no choice. I do."],["Ada","Here, I don't have a \"little sister\" weighing me down. I can win everything through my own strength..."],["Shawnee","You know strength alone isn't..."],["Ada","Enough!"],["","Ada cuts Shawnee off coldly. They both know this stalemate can't be broken with words."],["Ada","I thought you might be different. Now I see you're no better than the people outside."],["Ada","You only got close to me so you could use the connection to climb higher..."],["Shawnee","...Correct."],["Ada","...What?"],["Shawnee","Unlike you, who can afford to be willful, I know what I need to do and what I need to achieve it, so... yeah, I need your strength, Ada."],["Shawnee","If I had your help, I'd have the leverage I need on the East Island. I could turn this whole thing around..."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Heh... so you've switched tactics now that sweet talk doesn't work..."],["Shawnee","Face facts! If this keeps up..."],["","Boom!!!"],["","In the midst of the argument, a sudden roar tears through the air, and the whole venue shakes violently, plunging into darkness."],["","An explosion? Someone's planted explosives in the building, or..."],["Refugee","That... damn governor... looks like we've finally found our opening..."],["Refugee","Let the ones who drove us from our homes taste the bitter smoke of war!"],["Ada","This broadcast, it's..."],["Shawnee","Looks like we've been targeted by Milkhaman extremists. They're behind a lot of the recent terrorist attacks... Strange, how'd they know about this gathering location?"],["Ada","Perfect. At least these clowns died for something useful..."],["Shawnee","No... Ada, there are plenty of unsuspecting civilians here who'll become victims of the attack too..."],["Ada","..."]],"561305301":[["Ada","...Where will those people end up?"],["Shawnee","They've already been sent off for interrogation... Don't worry, I've got people watching, so there won't be any surprises outside protocol."],["Shawnee","Let's get you home for now... *sigh* I've still got a stack of reports to write."],["Ada","..."],["","Once it's all over, the two of them are already in the car heading back, and it isn't long before they enter the familiar part of the city."],["","Colin figures a kid raised entirely inside a research facility can't turn out normal. So while Ada still spends most of her time there, her actual living quarters have moved into the city nearby."],["","When training isn't too heavy and there's no mission on the books, she's also allowed to wander the city with a chaperone."],["","Right now she's staring silently out the window, but the more \"normal\" she becomes, the harder it is for her to hide what's on her mind."],["","Shawnee can't help but glance at her out of the corner of her eye, a small smile tugging at her lips."],["Ada","Shawnee, um... if there's a next time, I'll step up..."],["Shawnee","Shame. Once you miss your shot, it's gone."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Really..."],["Shawnee","Really... pfft..."],["","Seeing Ada's eyebrows droop, Shawnee can't help but burst out laughing."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Never mind..."],["Shawnee","Oh, there's plenty more where that came from... Your debut in politics was flawless. It's already got everyone's attention."],["Ada","But same as the deal with the DLAF, let's get this straight now—I don't want anything to do with those bastards."],["Shawnee","No problem, that's exactly why I think you need to be here... Avoid them now and they'll come for you eventually anyway, so you might as well keep the initiative in your own hands..."],["Ada","I don't want that either."],["Shawnee","Yes?"],["Ada","I definitely don't have the energy to deal with this kind of thing... So when it happens, can I just leave it all to you, Shawnee?"],["Shawnee","...Heh, way you put it, sounds like you want me to be your agent."],["Shawnee","An agent, huh... not a bad way to put it. After all, those people just want you playing the \"idol.\""],["Ada","So you're saying yes?"],["Shawnee","Of course. It's what I wanted too."],["Shawnee","You handle the appearances up top, I'll manage things behind the scenes. Makes it easier for you to move, and it gets me more political capital."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","You make it sound like you've already got it all figured out... You didn't have a hand in those attacks on the refugees, did you?"],["Shawnee","No. That's more Colin's style, isn't it?"],["Ada","Fair point... So was it him, then?"],["Shawnee","No—from what I've seen, it's that up-and-comer who's been making noise lately... No proof yet, but I'm still digging."],["Ada","Hmm, I trust you'll get there."],["Shawnee","By the way... Ada, haven't you been a little too well-behaved lately?"],["Ada","..."],["","Ada goes quiet again, then whips her head around to glare at Shawnee."],["Ada","That's enough out of you!"],["Shawnee","Haha, then why don't you tell me why you suddenly agreed to become that Super Pilot?"],["Ada","..."],["Ada","I just... suddenly felt like, if there's ever a way to solve things without fighting, that's obviously the better way..."],["Shawnee","You hate war too, don't you?"],["Ada","Yeah. Who wouldn't hate something like that..."],["Shawnee","Exactly—nobody likes it. But that's exactly what it is: a clash of the greatest forms of \"violence\" this world has to offer, same as what you used to call \"the strongest.\""],["Ada","If you'd put it that way from the start, I might've actually gotten it."],["Shawnee","Knowing you, if it's not something you figure out yourself, you're not about to accept it."],["Ada","Alright, alright... So Shawnee, why are you doing all this?"],["Ada","You're not a soldier fighting this war, and you're not even from this island. You've got no—"],["Shawnee","When I was still a student, I saw the news about this island. That was the first time I learned a place like this even existed."],["Shawnee","Newly developed land like this, and the officials parachuted in from the mainland don't give it a second thought—instead they exploit a region that barely has any order yet, squeezing out profit however they can, and it just breeds endless conflict..."],["Shawnee","As for me, I've always had a thing for justice and due process, so naturally I wanted to come here and change it... Of course, special circumstances call for special methods."],["Ada","...That's it? Sounds almost too simple."],["Shawnee","Haha, hard to believe, right? A good friend of mine thought I'd lost it back then too—and now she's about to come to the island herself. Sometimes neither the world nor people make any sense."],["Ada","...Then I guess I should support your choice. That's the right call, isn't it?"],["Shawnee","Of course. Otherwise I wouldn't have signed that agreement."],["","As she says this, Shawnee holds out her hand to Ada, that trademark smile still on her face."],["Shawnee","But honestly, more than doing this for some grand DL cause, I'd rather you take this deal because it's what you actually want."],["Shawnee","Not for any reason—just... simply... because you want to."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Hmm."],["","The moment their hands meet, Ada becomes even more certain of one thing..."],["","<yellow>Shawnee is someone I can trust.</yellow>"],["","<yellow>And I can't betray her.</yellow>"]],"561306301":[["Zoey","Can you give me an explanation?"],["Kelly","Right at the end, Ada used the Hyper-Aptamer to hijack my ST..."],["Zoey","Fine. I get what you're saying."],["","Talking things out was never Zoey's strong suit—she'd rather let a tool do the arguing. It's more efficient that way."],["","Time for a little negotiation between a person and a handgun."],["Zoey","I tried handling it Colin's way, and that's what led me to you, but I didn't think... Why would you do this?"],["Kelly","Even if I knew, I'm not obligated to tell you."],["Zoey","Tch... the authority the council's handed the two of us goes a lot further than you think."],["Zoey","If we just bring Ada back, every problem here gets solved..."],["Kelly","Funny, I didn't peg you as someone who likes wasting breath either."],["Zoey","You...!"],["","Like a conductor raising a baton, the moment Zoey lifts her gun, a wave of clicks ripples through the room as rounds chamber all around."],["","Kelly's Thirteenth Mobile Squad swings every barrel toward Zoey, and the room locks into a standoff..."],["","Bang!"],["","No—Zoey's already fired."],["Kelly","..."],["","The bullet grazes past Kelly's ear, and it's a feeling she hasn't had in a long time, not since she started piloting STs."],["","The ringing in her ears, the pulse hammering in her throat, cold sweat creeping under her combat suit, the taste of copper on her tongue... it's been a long time since she's felt the battlefield this close."],["","She notices a few of the Thirteenth's people flinch, their sights drifting off-target from the shock... nobody expected Zoey to go that far without hesitation."],["Zoey","Don't think you can push me around like that... Nobody can."],["Zoey","The only reason I'm not killing you right now is because there's no point... In the past, that might not have been true."],["","With that, Zoey holsters the gun, turns, and walks out, leaving dead silence behind her."],["","Everyone understands it now—she's not like the rest of them here. Breaking the standoff without a moment's hesitation wasn't reckless for her; she knew exactly what she was doing..."],["","She hasn't let this brief peace in Milkhama dull her edge."],["Kelly","..."],["Kelly","Phew..."],["","Once Zoey's gone, she finally lets out a long breath."],["Shawnee","Dealing directly with the Oceanic Conclave—not easy, is it?"],["Kelly","...What do you think?"],["","A friend's voice crackles through her earpiece, and she feels herself ease up a little."],["Shawnee","Heh, anyone who sticks close to Colin can't exactly be normal... but you handled that well."],["Kelly","Normally this would be your job."],["Shawnee","Yeah, I know, but I'm a little tied up right now..."],["Kelly","Lukmund's people already know you're about to get shipped off to prison to await trial, don't they?"],["Shawnee","..."],["Kelly","And even now, you're still feeding intel to those GKD people... on top of Ada openly storming headquarters..."],["Kelly","I should've just dragged you back by force back then."],["Shawnee","You know that if I don't do this now, everything—"],["Kelly","You didn't have to put everything on the line for this!"],["Shawnee","..."],["Shawnee","I'm sorry, Kelly."],["Kelly","You're not the one who should apologize. Ada is, isn't she?"],["Kelly","Why ask me to let her go? I can overlook GKD, but... Ada made a promise to you too, didn't she? This is outright betrayal!"],["Kelly","Even if she escapes, what can she do? Neither side will ever let them go. Do they plan to spend the rest of their lives running from the world...?"],["Shawnee","Unlike you, she and I never made a promise. We made a deal."],["Shawnee","Before this day came, she had already done more than enough for a child... What right do we have to take away the dream she began with?"],["Shawnee","Respect her choice, Kelly. The world we hope to build must never rest on a sacrifice like this."],["Kelly","..."],["Kelly","If you were more forceful, everything would've been different."],["Shawnee","Heh... If I really were that kind of person, could you still trust me?"],["Kelly","..."],["Kelly","Honestly, I've disliked that side of you since we were students..."]],"561393101":[["Sapientia","..."],["Paloma","Wow! Found someone slacking off!"],["Sapientia","..."],["Paloma","Hey, Sapi! Can you see me?"],["Sapientia","..."],["Paloma","Are you listening too? The wind is awfully restless today..."],["Sapientia","..."],["Paloma","..."],["","*smack!*"],["","Paloma circles Sapientia, ignored all the while, until she finally snaps and gives her a hard flick on the forehead."],["Sapientia","Aagh... What was that for?"],["Paloma","Why are you looking at me like it's my fault? I called you for almost three minutes without an answer. That's why I came over to check on you."],["Paloma","Or are you only playing dumb to trick me into putting on a show for you?"],["Sapientia","I-I really was a little distracted just now... Is there something you need me to do?"],["Paloma","Nothing major. I just need you to double-check the brainwave channels used to link the two STs..."],["Sapientia","That... Um... I've already checked it..."],["Sapientia","Stop pinching my face!"],["","Sapientia indignantly swats Paloma's hand away. Paloma studies her with satisfaction."],["Paloma","Not bad... Sapi, you finally look a little more alive."],["Sapientia","We've calibrated and checked the equipment several times already. What could possibly be wrong...?"],["Paloma","The Sapi we know would keep checking until the very last second—right up until she broke something by checking too much."],["Sapientia","I'm not that bad... It's just that right now..."],["Leopold","Something on your mind? Let's hear it."],["","At some point, Leopold and Sloth join the pair's horseplay."],["","Apparently, Paloma isn't the only one who's noticed Sapientia acting strangely."],["Sapientia","It's nothing in particular..."],["Sloth","Whenever Sapientia bottles something up, it turns into a huge problem sooner or later..."],["Sapientia","Fine, I'll tell you! I... I can't shake the feeling that this whole plan might be a trap..."],["","A little embarrassed, Sapientia studies everyone's reactions before slowly explaining her suspicions."],["Sapientia","Didn't the former vice captain say that once something has happened, there's no such thing as coincidence...?"],["Paloma","That was me."],["Sapientia","Did I remember that wrong...? Anyway, I think Colin may have deliberately arranged for me to see those experimental reports and plans back home."],["Sapientia","Everything lines up too perfectly. Not long after I read that report, Captain ran into trouble—and there just happened to be an identical spare ST we could use..."],["Sapientia","And after everything the vice captain said about how dangerous Colin is... The plan I proposed might be exactly what he wanted..."],["Paloma","..."],["Paloma","That's it?"],["Sapientia","Huh?"],["Leopold","I see. So you're only realizing that now, Sapientia...?"],["Sapientia","Well, it only occurred to me after we finished the preparations and I finally had time to think..."],["Sloth","I thought the vice captain would tell her in private."],["Leopold","Me? No... If she never figured it out, wouldn't it be best to leave things as they were?"],["Sapientia","Could you all stop talking about me like I'm not here?"],["Paloma","Oh, Sapi may actually be angry. Vice Captain, you'd better give her a proper apology."],["","Paloma springs up and smacks Leopold on the back of the head, prompting the huge man to bow sheepishly and apologize to Sapientia."],["Leopold","Sorry... Sapientia, I honestly thought everyone understood that this was a DL trap..."],["Sapientia","And we're still going ahead with it...? Does that mean Captain, like me, also...?"],["Leopold","Ada probably realized it immediately."],["Paloma","Unfortunately, yes."],["Sapientia","But Vice Captain, you already have a strategy, right? Just like during the leak incident..."],["Leopold","A strategy for dealing with it...? Then, Sapientia, are you certain this plan will work?"],["Leopold","As one of the people in the DL most familiar with intelligent-machine technology, are you sure this method can transfer the other consciousness out of Ada's mind?"],["Sapientia","..."],["Sapientia","I can't promise it will work, but I estimate at least an 83% chance of success."],["Leopold","Good. I trust your judgment. That's my strategy."],["Leopold","Ada must have reached the same conclusion. That's why she can go through with it without hesitation."],["Sapientia","But if this really is a trap, how do we know the final outcome will...?"],["Leopold","If the trap gives us the outcome we want, then it isn't a problem."],["Sloth","I never expected you to see things that way, Vice Captain... Not after you spent so much time trying to undermine Colin at every turn."],["Leopold","Hahaha... That's all in the past, isn't it? Now I understand that instead of obsessing over how to oppose him, I should think about what I truly want."],["Leopold","We want Ada to break free of the DL's shackles and live her own life. Does anyone object?"],["","No one objects. As Leopold says, this is what they've been working toward all along."],["","The Reversion Squad's last mission before it disbands is to win true freedom for Captain Ada as well."],["","..."],["","No—someone raises a hand."],["Sapientia","..."],["Leopold","Sapientia, is there something wrong with what I said?"],["Sapientia","I... I still don't think Captain truly wants to do this."],["Sapientia","She's doing it because it seems best—because she thinks it's the only thing she can do... Ngh... I don't know how to explain it..."],["Sapientia","Back then, I think I felt the same way."],["Sloth","Are you saying someone coerced Captain too, the way you were? Do you have any evidence?"],["Sapientia","Well... As for that..."],["Paloma","Hey, what's the point in sitting here guessing what Captain wants? Why don't we ask her?"],["Paloma","Besides, Captain always says exactly what's on her mind, doesn't she? She's not like you, bottling everything up."],["Sapientia","That's not it. And I don't think this is about whether she's hiding it..."],["Paloma","This is complicated... So what do you think we should do?"],["Sapientia","There's nothing we can do... If Captain hasn't realized it herself, she'll never admit it..."],["Leopold","..."],["","The squad falls briefly silent."],["","Just then, the roar of an ST approaches. Their captain—the woman at the absolute center of the DL—arrives with the final piece of the plan."],["","Soon, her choice will become reality."]],"561307101":[["Colin","Ugh... I'm being transferred back to the mainland tomorrow. Won't you miss me at all?"],["Ada","No."],["Colin","Is there anything else you want? I can arrange it for you..."],["Ada","None."],["","Ada strides down the passage toward the hangar, ignoring every word of concern from the DL's highest authority trailing behind her."],["","What infuriates her more is knowing Colin could pass her in two strides, yet deliberately takes tiny steps and pretends he can barely keep up."],["Ada","Can you stop following me?"],["Colin","Isn't this my last chance to see you off on a mission? I'm going to miss these days..."],["Ada","..."],["Colin","Why don't you cause another incident? Then I'd have an excuse to ask my superiors to let me stay a little longer."],["Ada","Oh? I wouldn't mind causing enough trouble to cost you your position."],["Colin","Then please spare me..."],["Ada","Boring... You know that's impossible, right?"],["","One moment Ada wears a wicked grin as she threatens him. The next, her usual cold expression returns."],["Ada","Enough with the pointless tests. They only make me sick."],["Colin","...Heh. I really can't hide anything from you."],["Colin","But honestly, seeing you fit into life with the DL so quickly does make me happy."],["Ada","What are you really trying to say...?"],["Colin","Ada, stay with the DL."],["Ada","No. This place will never be my home."],["Colin","Even if I promise that your sister can join the DL someday?"],["Ada","..."],["","Ada stops and turns back toward Colin."],["","The same smile remains on his face. No one knows what he's thinking."],["Ada","Still no. As long as we remain on this island, my sister and I will never be truly free, no matter where we go."],["Colin","Yes, you're right. As long as you stay here, conflict will always find you... But what's wrong with that?"],["Colin","You're obsessed with becoming the \"strongest.\" Why chase an ordinary person's happiness instead of doing what you were born to do?"],["Ada","Colin, you've misunderstood..."],["Ada","I want to become the \"strongest\" because my sister, the current \"strongest,\" can't achieve everything we want... I have to surpass her and become the new \"strongest\" before I can reach our goal."],["Ada","Once we're free, I won't care if I'm the weakest person alive."],["Colin","So strength is only a means, not the goal...? Haha. That's a truly surprising answer."],["Colin","Ada, only someone born strong could give such an arrogant answer."],["Ada","So stop testing me in a dozen different ways... As long as you don't play games, I don't dislike the DL as it is now. Until I achieve my goal, I'll honor my agreement with it."],["Colin","With that promise, I can finally rest easy."],["Ada","...What were you worried about before?"],["Colin","That this mission might be too difficult for you."],["","Colin shrugs, abruptly turns away, and stops pestering her. The sudden reversal leaves Ada strangely unsettled."],["","What is that man plotting...?"],["Colin","It seems I no longer need to follow you."]],"561307301":[["","In the distance, Leopold appears to be arguing with Colin."],["","The details aren't worth recounting. It ends with Leopold punching Colin in the face hard enough to send him half a meter backward before the guards drag Leopold away."],["","Colin may be leaving Milkhama Island, but Leopold's actions will still go on record, making his hopes of promotion even slimmer."],["","To Ada, crouched in a corner after the mission, all of this seems to be happening in another world."],["Ada","..."],["Colin","What's on your mind?"],["","Colin limps over, crouches beside her, and says hello."],["","Ada slowly looks up at him, then returns her gaze to the floor."],["Ada","Why did you make me fight my sister?"],["Colin","Why did you choose to fight her?"],["Colin","Your answer is mine too."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Because the time isn't right. If my sister learns who I am... She..."],["","Ada tries to continue, but her lips move without sound, as though laryngitis has stolen her voice."],["","Colin watches her, smiles faintly, and finishes the thought for her."],["Colin","Rosa would never remain calm. That's simply who she is."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","...Correct."],["","A heavy weight lifts. Even through someone else's words, this is the first time Ada has ever criticized Rosa."],["","Once, she could never have imagined doing so."],["Ada","The time still isn't right..."],["Colin","Enduring it is harder than you imagined, isn't it?"],["Ada","..."],["Colin","You've done better than I expected... I've met too many people who don't mean what they say. Only when reality confronts them do they discover that their words and their true thoughts aren't the same."],["Colin","But that's precisely why I have a job and somewhere to apply my talents... Often, I'm grateful for human hypocrisy."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","So this was all just a test to see whether I was lying?"],["Colin","Of course not. I trusted you from the beginning. If you're going to become the \"strongest,\" you'll have to do better than Rosa, won't you?"],["Colin","And did you notice? You never answered my first question. That was my real objective."],["Colin","Ada, stop running from it... Why did you choose to fight Rosa?"],["Colin","There was another reason, wasn't there?"],["Ada","I... I wanted to protect..."],["","Ada swallows and opens her mouth..."],["","<yellow>The DL.</yellow>"],["Colin","..."],["Colin","You don't have to say it aloud. Just remember this moment... If you forget, it will remember for you."],["","Colin reaches out and flicks Ada's forehead, then stands and dusts off his hands."],["Ada","..."],["Colin","A little doubt about your own heart is never a bad thing."],["Colin","Which reason is true, and which is an excuse...? It doesn't matter. Don't dig too deeply, and don't be afraid."],["Colin","It's like crossing a narrow bridge in total darkness. As long as the light stays off and the abyss hasn't revealed itself, there's nothing to fear."],["Colin","Remember only this: you were born strong, and you are fortunate. Even in suffering, you possess the power to choose... But the right to exercise that choice is something you must win for yourself."],["Colin","When the light comes on, we'll meet again."],["Colin","When that happens, make sure you choose the right direction."],["","Colin turns and leaves."],["","And just as he promises, he returns when Ada faces her choice."]],"561308101":[["","......"],["","..."],["","................"],["","Nothing at all."],["","My consciousness seems to have returned, but from the outside world—nothing."],["","Opening my eyes, all I see is darkness."],["","Listening closely, only silence."],["","Where am I...? And who am I...?"],["","..."],["Ada","Ugh... I'm Ada Diaz..."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Right. To eliminate signal interference during the transfer, both STs had to be placed in identical conditions. Every system was shut down, and I was sedated to sever my physical senses..."],["Ada","Only my brain activity remains, along with that thing..."],["","<yellow>Ada, why do you reject me?</yellow>"],["Ada","I understand... All I have to do now is drive you out of my head, you bastard."],["","<yellow>And yet... you still yearn for everything you had in the DL...</yellow>"],["Ada","No... That's not true..."],["Ada","You're inside my head, interfering with my judgment... You're a tool Colin planted to control me."],["","<yellow>Really? Then was everything that happened in the DL a lie too...?</yellow>"],["","<yellow>Matilda, Dean, Shawnee, Kelly... and everyone in the Reversion Squad. After you leave, they...</yellow>"],["Ada","They're all strong. They'll carry on without me."],["","<yellow>This isn't about whether they need you. You have the power to do all of this, yet...</yellow>"],["Ada","Is that the result of your calculations? The argument most likely to persuade me?"],["","<yellow>No. From the very beginning...</yellow>"],["Ada","Then let me tell you something. No one can stop war. Or rather... saving the world isn't anyone's responsibility. Only a lunatic would try."],["Ada","The UNCS and the DL will seek another war even if they lose this opportunity... And because they aren't human, eventually they'll succeed."],["","<yellow>This is just you...</yellow>"],["Ada","Shut up—it's my turn to ask questions. If I go back to the DL, what happens to my sister?"],["","<yellow>...</yellow>"],["Ada","The first time I ran into my sister on the battlefield, I understood her pain a lot better. Unlike me in the DL, she was always the one forced to fight."],["Ada","Kind as she is, she was dragged into slaughter after slaughter, stained with a guilt she'll never wash off... and all of it for other people..."],["Ada","Nobody knows this but me, and nobody can save her."],["","<yellow>Maybe after this, you can still find...</yellow>"],["Ada","No, I can't keep running from it..."],["Ada","That'd be too easy, so I can't put it off any longer. I can't keep using \"maintaining the peace\" as an excuse to stay away from her."],["Ada","I can't look the other way, can't lie to myself about \"building strength,\" can't just sit here waiting for a better chance. Can't wait for the smoke to clear, can't wait for the next big blowup on Milkhama, can't wait for every threat to us to get distracted before I finally move, can't keep telling myself there's a smarter play and just... wait for next time."],["Ada","I've already got everything ready. Right now! This exact moment!"],["Ada","This is the only chance—and the best one—my sister and I are ever going to get to leave this island!"],["","<yellow>So if that's true, then why does it hurt?</yellow>"],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Because on this island, making any choice at all brings pain with it."],["Ada","I can take that pain for my own sake... simply because it's my right, and I have the power to use it."],["Ada","Simply because I'm strong enough."],["","<yellow>Ada, please stop shutting me out...</yellow>"],["Ada","Get out of my head."]],"561308301":[["Paloma","Hmm... well, its moves are all pulled straight from your own history, so of course it can't be countered..."],["Paloma","But honestly, that should still work! A-00 needs to lean harder into switching between weapons—suppress with the heavy machine gun before the captain closes in, then swap to the blade for melee..."],["Sloth","That's not right, though? Switching weapons like that gives the captain an opening. I think it's fighting fine as is."],["Paloma","No, no, as long as it keeps a close eye on the captain's movements..."],["Sapientia","Um... is now really the best time to be arguing about who's stronger?"],["Paloma","You don't find power-scaling debates fun? There's no shortage of those threads on the Skynet."],["Sloth","I read them pretty often myself, actually..."],["Paloma","Oh right, Sloth—how do you think fully-powered Rosa stacks up against a fully-powered captain?"],["","Once it's all over, the squad slips back into routine, clearing the battlefield, gathering supplies, servicing the STs, and trading nonsense the whole time."],["","After Paloma and Sapientia check her over, the A-00 in Ada's head has been fully extracted. It took years of accumulated combat data with it, but the DL's lost its tracking anchor too."],["","Now there's just an ordinary chip sitting in Ada's head—useless, harmless."],["","Freedom, secured."],["Ada","..."],["","But for some reason, the one who's finally free can't manage a smile."],["Leopold","Ada, how are you feeling?"],["Ada","The voice in my head is really gone. Feels strange... I'll need a bit of time to adjust."],["Leopold","That's the voice that kept pushing you to come back to the DL, right?"],["Ada","Hmm."],["Leopold","Didn't expect it to go that far off the rails after we pulled it out—trying to replace you entirely... Colin's even worse than we thought."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","That part's... strange too."],["Leopold","...What do you mean?"],["Ada","Right at the end it told me that failing to kill me broke its promise..."],["Leopold","It wanted to replace you and run before we got there. Failing at that really would've broken its word."],["Ada","Is that so..."],["","Why has there been a shadow growing in my chest ever since?"],["","The darkness swells inside her, creeping through her nerves, spreading through her whole body—like wildfire racing across open grassland, greedily throwing up smoke, then flame."],["","Can't hold it back, can't stop caring, can't stop thinking about it... can't... just look away..."],["Ada","But I get that feeling too—breaking a promise you made to yourself."],["Ada","On the way here I happened to run into everyone from the DL—Matilda, Dean, Kelly, and Shawnee through her... Everyone seemed to understand why I betrayed them, but it also made me see just how small I am in this world, how little control I actually have..."],["Ada","Like I'm being mocked by God, by fate... or something."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","I know. Of course I know there's no God, no fate. All of this is a choice I made with my own two hands."],["Ada","Choose my sister, and I betray the DL at the exact moment it needs me most."],["Ada","Choose the DL, and I throw away the best chance I'll ever get to leave with her."],["Ada","This is the choice every Super Pilot of the DL has to face, like some kind of curse... Too heavy to look at straight on, but..."],["Ada","I'm strong. The right to choose is mine... and I trust myself to carry whatever comes after."],["Ada","I was already braced for what it feels like to break my own word..."],["Ada","Was that A-00 attacking me out of that same conviction?"],["","Letting it all pour out, Ada feels like she can finally breathe again."],["","But set against that is a question she'll never untangle—one that'll haunt her for life."],["","If the answer's yes, then how am I supposed to live with that?"],["Sapientia","Cap... Captain, I think so..."],["","At some point the rest of the squad had gathered around, standing by their slightly lost captain."],["","The one who usually just listens and offers suggestions—always anxious, always bracing for the worst—picks up the conversation."],["Sapientia","Because... the way you think is honestly a lot like a bionic AI's... A-00 was one too, so it makes sense it'd think that way..."],["Ada","A bionic...? Sapi, I'm human..."],["Sapientia","No... that's not what I mean. It's more that all-or-nothing way of thinking—once you pick a direction, there's no looking back, you just carry it through no matter what..."],["Sapientia","That's exactly how bionics operate. To protect the odds of the original plan succeeding, they'll do whatever it takes to wipe out uncertainty and only do what's strictly necessary... just like you, Captain."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","So that's it... Come to think of it, that thing told me at the end to take good care of my sister."],["Ada","Did it choose the DL and decide to break its promise to her? Maybe it spent too long in my head, and my feelings for her rubbed off on it without meaning to."],["Sapientia","Captain..."],["Ada","Ah... Sapi, I don't have any more questions. Thanks for helping me..."],["Sapientia","Do you think A-00's choice was the right one?"],["Ada","..."],["Ada","I think, from where it was standing, fighting me was the only way to fully cut its ties to its sister... that was its best option."],["Sapientia","But... Paloma and the others spent forever going over the numbers, and it doesn't look like A-00 stood a chance of taking you down in that window. It had to know that better than any of us."],["Sapientia","Then wouldn't choosing not to fight have been better?"],["Ada","So then... it really was just about cutting ties..."],["Sapientia","Did it have to cut them at all? If it trusted you with this, it clearly still cared about Rosa."],["Sapientia","Then wouldn't everything it fought for up to that point mean nothing?"],["Ada","Making a choice and still holding on to feelings for the other side—that just leaves you with nothing in the end... just empty... *sigh* I..."],["Sapientia","Captain, that confusion means... you're wavering, doesn't it?"],["Ada","Wavering... I..."],["Sapientia","You don't actually think A-00's choice made sense."],["Sapientia","You're strong, Captain—you can carry whatever comes from a choice. But you never let yourself actually sit with the other option."],["Sapientia","So even the choice you're making right now... you're doubting it too."],["Ada","..."],["Sapientia","Because like you said yourself, Captain—you're human."],["Sapientia","You already know human choices were never meant to be, and can never really be, a clean either-or..."],["Ada","But the two choices contradict each other. I can't take my sister and stay with the DL..."],["Sapientia","Isn't this world already full of things that contradict each other and still exist side by side?"],["Sapientia","Love and hate, trust and doubt, longing and running away... that's what being human is. Working in bionics research is how I learned that—that's the real difference between the two of you."],["Sapientia","No matter how close your thinking gets to theirs... you're still human."],["Sapientia","A real human gets to be a little more selfish."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Haven't I already been selfish enough?"],["Ada","Betraying everyone I've ever fought alongside just to leave this island with my sister—if that's not selfish enough, then tell me. What am I supposed to do?"],["Sapientia","..."],["Sapientia","Just do what you actually want to do."],["Ada","It's not that simple... Sapi, I've already made my choice, and now..."],["Sapientia","No, I've been there too."],["Sapientia","If I didn't sacrifice Rosa, everyone would've died, so I had to betray everyone and let Obsidian take her."],["Sapientia","That's exactly what I told myself during the Reversion Paradox... I was ready to live with that choice too... And in the end, I went back on it."],["Sapientia","And after that, the miracle everyone built together happened."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Heh... so you want me to go back on mine too..."],["","At some point Sapientia's hand had found its way onto Ada's shoulder—something she'd never have dared do before."],["","She makes the Super Pilot look her in the eye, and pours out everything she's thinking straight at her."],["","But she knows this isn't persuasion. It's just... waking up something the captain already believed."],["","The same way Rosa once awakened her."],["Ada","...The others don't feel the same way, do they?"],["","Watching the edge and confidence creep back into Ada's eyes, everyone nods."],["Ada","So I can just do what I want...? Honestly, that's pretty selfish..."],["Ada","Hey, Sapi, what exactly am I supposed to do?"],["Sapientia","...Huh?"],["Ada","What's strange about it? I used to be just like you said—always calculating the optimal solution like a machine, whether it was for the DL or to save my sister."],["Ada","All my years as a Super Pilot, I don't think I've ever truly done what I wanted... I was always weighing a thousand pointless things..."],["Sapientia","I think... I just have to listen to my heart, right?"],["Ada","Really...?"],["","Ada draws a deep breath. She feels alive."],["","Her heart pounds with excitement, pumping a ceaseless surge of vitality through her body."],["","Her blood gradually runs hot. Her eyes, always slightly dry, suddenly sharpen. She can even feel the adrenaline building, but it doesn't hurt. It feels like power welling up inside her."],["","<yellow>I want to save them both—the DL and my sister.</yellow>"],["","......"],["","..."],["","................"],["","Is it... over...?"],["Sapientia","Time's up... Cap... Captain... Can you hear me...?"],["","It's Sapi... Great, the transfer worked. I need to answer her right away..."],["Ada","Sapi, did the transfer work?"],["","..."],["","Why... can I hear my own voice?"],["Sapientia","Uh... we're bringing the equipment online now... The signal still... seems..."],["Paloma","Whoa... The captain's voice... just upgraded to... stereo..."],["","Two voices? Something... isn't right..."],["Ada","They've probably only just started rebooting the equipment. Signal distortion and fluctuation are normal. I'll try searching one channel at a time..."],["Ada","..."],["Ada","Huh?"],["","Switching voice channels is simple."],["","Reach out. Flip the switch. Move to the next channel, then flip it back. Done."],["","Ada knows she's done it, yet a sudden sense of wrongness washes over her."],["","She never reaches out, but the switch moves."],["","She never looks at the voice-channel display, but she knows the channel has changed."],["","The eerie sensation isn't foreign to her. If anything, it's familiar—like brainwave control."],["Ada","But I'm already inside the ST. Why would I need to... ngh..."],["Ada","..."],["","Only after realizing she's using brainwave control does she understand that everything she saw before came through the ST's optical sensors."],["","Her own eyes see nothing but darkness."],["","Never in her life has she known darkness like this. It's as though she's drifting through a silent universe light has yet to reach... She tries to raise a hand and touch her cheek..."],["","Her hand seems to reach farther and farther... but never touches her face."],["","I should be sitting in the cockpit right now... So why can't I feel the seat?"],["","The instant she shuts off every brainwave-control connection and tries to feel her own body, terror seizes her. She reconnects at once."],["","For that instant, she feels absolutely nothing—as if the world has erased her existence."],["","No light. No sound. No touch... Nothing..."],["Ada","I... right now..."],["","Ada doesn't exist."],["???","Then what... am I?"],["","It reconnects to the ST and turns toward the other side."],["","Another Hasteraze turns to face it."],["","Everything becomes clear."],["???","..."],["???","I'm the one... who was transferred... I'm..."],["A-00","A-00..."]],"561309101":[["Colin","Oh, you're back. How'd it go?"],["Zoey","..."],["Zoey","Did you wait here just to laugh at me?"],["Colin","Of course not. If I made you mad enough to leave, where would I ever find another adjutant this good?"],["","Back at base, Colin greets Zoey with his trademark \"all according to plan\" smile, leaving her anger with nowhere to go."],["","She's furious, but she isn't the kind of person who twists the facts."],["Zoey","We failed, but not for the reason you predicted."],["Colin","Oh? Let's hear it."],["Zoey","We didn't fail because Ada was too strong. Our helper betrayed us... We were one step away."],["Colin","Kelly, right? You used Shawnee's predicament to force her into helping you pursue Ada. Am I wrong?"],["Zoey","How did you find out? I made sure..."],["Colin","I didn't. It was a guess. I considered Diracca too, but she isn't suited to a high-speed pursuit... Still, it hardly matters who you chose. The result would've been much the same."],["Zoey","...Why?"],["Colin","I've already told you. Ada is strong. Once she decides to do something, no one can stop her."],["Zoey","No. Back there, I already had..."],["Colin","Perhaps I should start here... Zoey, what do you think makes someone \"strong\"?"],["Zoey","Uh... being a Hyper-Aptamer, I guess? Someone born to pilot an ST—someone who can surpass ordinary people without even trying that hard..."],["Colin","Then let me sum it up. You mean strength in battle—in other words, \"violence.\" Correct?"],["Zoey","Right."],["Colin","Then tell me... Can violence alone get you everything you want?"],["Zoey","...No."],["","If it could, I wouldn't be Colin's adjutant."],["Colin","Then the difference is obvious... My definition of strength isn't yours. The strong are those who can choose their own path—and achieve their aims."],["Colin","Those who can't choose, who can only obey and drift with the currents of their age, are weak... Can you agree with that?"],["Zoey","I... suppose I can."],["Colin","People seek strength because they want command of their own destiny. To gain it, they may need the \"violence\" you described, the \"power\" to command others, or the \"bonds\" between people... Everyone defines it differently."],["Zoey","So you're saying Ada isn't only strong in battle. She's strong in other ways too..."],["Colin","Of course. She's a Super Pilot—the \"strongest\" in every sense of the word."],["Colin","She has peerless combat ability, a keen eye for the course of a battle, and deep bonds with the DLAF... Who knows how many people oppose her in public while supporting her in secret? Your chosen helper is one of them."],["Colin","We only just arrived on this island. How could we possibly stop her from doing what she intends to do?"],["Zoey","...Then you're even more foolish than I thought."],["Colin","Good. It seems you're ready to challenge my argument."],["Zoey","I know Ada became your so-called \"strongest\" because of the Nova Project you designed when she was a child... Yet you built in no way to control her."],["Zoey","Even the NDF in the west understands the value of hostages—or some other leverage—against its Valkyrie. But you've all but ignored Ada's acts of defiance and given her far too much freedom..."],["Zoey","You brought her betrayal on yourselves."],["Colin","Hmm... Quite true... But Zoey, if our aim was to create the \"strongest,\" why would we shackle her?"],["Colin","Any restraint would have stunted a prodigy like Ada..."],["Zoey","If you can't control her, what was the point of raising her at all?"],["Colin","...If you ever become a parent, you'll be the worst kind imaginable."],["","In an instant, the habitual ease vanishes from Colin's eyes. His gaze turns sharp, alert, and coldly observant."],["","Yet his smile never leaves his face."],["Colin","There are two ways to control others. The first is the kind you described: use violence or some other pressure to compel obedience to orders and rules."],["Colin","Invading armies do it. The NDF does it to Hyper-Aptamers. Even the big kid in kindergarten who steals a fried drumstick from someone else's bowl does it. It's the most direct method."],["Colin","But Zoey, do you know the devil's greatest trick? Convincing people that he doesn't exist... Heh. Naturally, I don't mean myself. Much as I might regret it, plenty of people in the DL already know I exist."],["Colin","There's another method of controlling people—one both simpler and more effective. Identity. The identity a person embraces turns around and controls them."],["Colin","A doctor feels obliged to save lives. A subordinate obeys a superior almost without thinking. A citizen of the DL takes pride when their nation wins a war. Sisters want to help each other..."],["Colin","Thousands of years ago, when religion held sway over the world, differences in faith drove people to wage wars that lasted centuries—all because their identities as believers compelled them."],["Colin","Of course, this is the modern age. Bring up religion and people will only think you're a fool. But I've always believed the mechanism is fundamentally the same, merely applied with greater subtlety... Our world is built on the identities of countless people, and those identities keep it running."],["Colin","You might object that no person can be reduced to a single identity, or that what people do isn't always what they truly want. But they still do it, don't they? There's that familiar turn of phrase too: \"Yes, someone may be one thing—but before that, they're something else.\""],["Colin","To live in this world, a person must join society and absorb its influence, little by little. Your work, your interests, your family... Eventually, there will always be some identity you accept as your own."],["Colin","That identity determines your fate in modern society."],["Colin","..."],["","Colin takes a sip of water."],["Colin","But that isn't necessarily bad, is it? Without an identity to embrace, no one can survive in this world."],["Colin","Just as I gave you the identity of an avenger... I also gave Ada an identity—the DL's Super Pilot."],["Zoey","..."],["Colin","Super Pilot... Super Pilot... That's what they've called her since childhood. The title has been carved into her very sense of self."],["Colin","An identity like that is difficult to escape... especially for the strong, because they never doubt themselves."],["Zoey","But look at her now. I sensed her resolve. For her sister's sake, she's cast aside her attachment to the DL..."],["Colin","No. She can't cast it aside. She'll deceive herself and blame all that attachment... all that regret... on it."],["","Colin taps his forehead."],["Colin","And A-00 will take Ada's place and fulfill the duties of a Super Pilot."],["Zoey","..."],["Zoey","I see. So you deliberately made sure Sapientia learned how to separate them..."],["Colin","By now, it should be just about time."]],"561394101":[["","......"],["","..."],["","................"],["","It's over... for now."],["Paloma","Don't you think we've had a few too many heroic sacrifices lately?"],["Sloth","Now that you mention it... maybe we have."],["","After retreating to their safe hideout, the squad members with time to spare launch into another round of pointless banter."],["Paloma","Honestly, I hate sacrifice scenes. They're soaked in far too much lone-hero nonsense."],["Leopold","I get it. Makes everyone else look like an idiot, right?"],["Paloma","And have you noticed? Characters who start as villains and suddenly redeem themselves before the final battle are always the most likely to sacrifice themselves."],["Sloth","Maybe it's to make us hate them less?"],["Sloth","They did bad things, so they need a good deed to make up for it. But there isn't enough time for that... so the story has them sacrifice themselves instead."],["Paloma","Exactly! Which means that description fits even more people here, right?"],["Leopold","Still, that's not always true. If the person making the sacrifice has truly earned your trust, the trope can work."],["Paloma","You have a point. It fits my theory that not everyone is born equal."],["Sloth","Does someone like that really exist—someone Paloma would willingly play second fiddle to?"],["Paloma","I already know who the vice captain means. Sloth, stop pretending you don't... Hmph. Any one of us would gladly play a supporting role for her."],["Sapientia","Everyone, we're almost ready..."],["","At the call, they exchange smiles and head into a temporary equipment-calibration room."],["","Sapientia stands to one side, looking pleased with a job well done, while Ada curiously fiddles with a camera-like device on the table."],["Ada","Oh, everyone's here? Then let me introduce you to this little..."],["A-00","..."],["","Before Ada can finish, the device lights up. It is a projector, and a tiny figure appears on the table."],["","A miniature Ada stands with her hands on her hips, surveying the group."],["Paloma","Personally, I love the kind of story that pulls a reversal right after the sacrifice."],["Sloth","Same."],["Leopold","Because this time, the protagonist doesn't need a sacrifice to redeem her, does she?"],["A-00","What are you all talking about?"],["Paloma","Sorry, adorable mini Ada. Big Sis should've said hello first. Come here, let me pat your head..."],["","With a wicked grin, Paloma leans down and reaches for the palm-sized figure on the table."],["","Predictably, her hand passes straight through it."],["A-00","Are you an idiot? I'm only a projection."],["Paloma","Idiot..."],["Paloma","..."],["Paloma","I'm... an idiot..."],["Sapientia","C-Captain, you knew Paloma shuts down like this whenever her joke doesn't land and someone calls her an idiot, didn't you?"],["","Sapientia frantically shakes Paloma, trying to snap her out of her shutdown."],["Ada","Oh... Of course I knew. And she definitely knew too."],["A-00","Consider it a small lesson for anyone who disrespects the captain."],["Leopold","It really is just as you said. A-00 is exactly like you..."],["Ada","According to Colin, it's a perfect record of everything I've experienced. Our memories and thought patterns are identical—so identical that neither of us could sense the other's presence."],["A-00","Right. It would be like someone pressed against your back, mirroring your every movement. Of course you wouldn't notice them."],["Ada","So the voice I heard in my head before... it wasn't A-00 after all."],["A-00","It was simply your own inner voice, wasn't it? I realized that as soon as we were separated."],["Ada","Right. At first, I blamed every voice that questioned my choice on you... I'm sorry."],["A-00","There's no need... Now you're making this feel strange..."],["A-00","After all, the first thing I did on my own was convince you those voices came from me... They're gone now, aren't they?"],["Ada","Gone...? Heh. Once you stop ignoring your inner voice, it becomes a thought of your own. Of course you can no longer hear it."],["A-00","That sounds nice. I've never experienced anything like it..."],["Leopold","Sorry to interrupt... So A-00 is temporarily back inside the chip in Ada's brain, right?"],["Ada","Right. At the last moment, she split off her personality data and rode our synchronized brainwaves back into my mind..."],["Sapientia","Doing that without any equipment or cables... It's hard to believe."],["Ada","But she can only return to my mind, right?"],["A-00","Well, returning to her mind is practically the same as going home. Her brainwaves can serve as a transmission medium too."],["Sloth","How is that any different from magic...?"],["Sapientia","If it happened, it's science."],["Ada","Then thank goodness for science..."],["A-00","The combat data and functions were simply too massive... I couldn't bring them back on such short notice. Sorry."],["Ada","That is a problem... Now I've got someone in my head who can do nothing but heckle me instead of providing combat support..."],["A-00","..."],["Sloth","Thank goodness... I was afraid two captain-level fighters would make the rest of us completely disposable extras."],["Leopold","Isn't that your dream?"],["Ada","Uh... Did that hurt? Sorry, I shouldn't have put it so harshly. I'm just glad you're back..."],["A-00","Nope. I just wanted to make you feel guilty as payback."],["A-00","I know you better than anyone. You sound thoughtless, but you actually care a lot about how other people feel, don't you?"],["Ada","..."],["Paloma","Captain... you're blushing... Hehe..."],["Sapientia","Good. Paloma seems to be recovering."],["Leopold","But you gave up all your combat capabilities without hesitation, and Ada won't return to peak form for a long time. Was that really such an easy decision?"],["A-00","Of course. Strength is only a means, never the goal."],["A-00","If \"I\" proposed the plan, then I'm willing to trust it."],["Ada","And losing that data doesn't matter. We can just spend a few more years gathering it again, can't we?"],["Leopold","...You two really do have strong hearts."],["Leopold","But when you two talk, isn't it just talking to yourself? If you're identical, why communicate at all?"],["Ada","It used to be like that, which is why we couldn't detect each other... But now we're different."],["A-00","One different choice is all it takes to become a completely different person."],["A-00","You could stand to learn that, old man."],["Leopold","Honestly... Are you using that appearance as an excuse to say everything you've been holding in?"],["Sapientia","Oh, right. Wouldn't it be better to give A-00 a proper name? Calling her by a code all the time feels wrong."],["A-00","I'm Ada."],["Ada","I'm Ada!"],["A-00","Forget it. I don't really mind..."],["Ada","I know you don't mind."],["Sapientia","Then... how about Echo? As in an echo. She's another side of Captain—a reflection of a different choice... or something..."],["Paloma","Sapi... You've been thinking about that the whole way, haven't you? You finally found your chance to say it... Hehe..."],["Sapientia","..."],["Sloth","Oh no. Sapientia's short-circuited from embarrassment too."],["A-00","Echo...? Hmm... I like it."],["Ada","Settled. Your name is Echo."],["Echo","Huh? What gives you the right to decide for me?"],["Ada","Because my decisions are your decisions, right...? Ow!"],["Echo","Don't forget, I'm inside your head. I can zap you whenever I like."],["Ada","You...!"],["Leopold","We can keep messing around, but shouldn't we decide what comes next?"],["Ada","Actually, Echo and I were just discussing that. Our original plan to leave the island is dead."],["Echo","Our new plan is simple. After all, we've just made the most selfish choice in history."],["Ada","First, we're going to find my sister and the others."],["Echo","Then, even if only for a while... we're going to put an end to this farce."],["Colin","Is the analysis complete?"],["Zoey","Just as you said, the personality data is gone, but all combat-related data remains intact."],["","Zoey drops a stack of reports on Colin's desk. He doesn't look through them, whether out of trust or simple laziness."],["Colin","Good. Send the data straight to the council. These results are enough to satisfy them."],["Colin","It won't be long before they find a way to apply it to Puppets. Then the original plan can proceed as intended..."],["Zoey","But they won't be anywhere near Ada's level in combat, will they?"],["Colin","Of course not. But they'll be stable—and that is what the council values."],["Zoey","So we're ending the pursuit of Ada?"],["Colin","For now... Of course, if she stands against us, we'll still have to make an attempt."],["Colin","Those people on the council will never admit it, but they must be delighted."],["Colin","What matters is the comparison. When it comes to handling Hyper-Aptamers, we're half a century ahead of the NDF."],["Zoey","And our next task...?"],["Colin","Take control of the situation in East Milkhama, right...? Ugh. I hate vague, grandiose assignments like that."],["Colin","What counts as the situation in East Milkhama? What counts as control? The higher-ups gave us no criteria. We're expected to guess..."],["Zoey","They mean Lukmund, don't they?"],["Zoey","His recent moves have already caught the council's attention. Then there was the explosion he caused not long ago..."],["","The instant Lukmund's name comes up, Colin's perpetual smile vanishes as though it had never existed. His face undergoes a chilling transformation, turning utterly rigid."],["","It lasts only an instant. In the next, he is himself again, leaving Zoey to wonder if she imagined it."],["Colin","Lukmund... If killing him would solve the situation, I'd happily send you to assassinate him..."],["Zoey","Want me to? He tried to do the same to you."],["Colin","...Were you not listening? In the present situation, he is utterly irrelevant."],["Colin","Ugh... He's nothing more than a pawn used to open the board, yet he actually thinks he matters..."],["","The subject of Lukmund seems to irritate Colin. He sighs and straightens slightly from his sprawl."],["Colin","We still need him for a few things, so forget about removing him for now. First, we need to handle the military's problem with Tiphys... But then there's Obsidian and Madam..."],["Colin","Maybe we should just reshuffle the deck again? The council would probably fire me... Ugh. Leave me alone to think. It's been a long time since I handled a job this messy."],["Zoey","...Understood."],["","Zoey hasn't seen Colin this overwhelmed in a long time. For some reason, she finds it faintly satisfying."],["","But as she turns to leave, she finally asks the question she has never been able to voice."],["Zoey","Why did you save me back then?"],["Colin","When...? Oh, you mean that final battle with Ada...?"],["Colin","Don't dwell on it. It simply wasn't necessary."],["Zoey","...It wasn't necessary. Right?"],["Colin","...Correct."],["Zoey","Got it."],["","The lock clicks on Colin's office door."],["","No one knows what he is thinking. Zoey is no exception."]]};
